{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QQikXYb83inveSYhsZPfcr","type":"tool_result","content":"578\t| `passFlair` (behind the back; 15%, always in Supernova) | .12 s | right hand sweeps [0, 5, 14] → [−3, −4, 14] |\n579\t| `catch` | until the ball arrives | both hands reach toward where the ball will be in .15 s |\n580\t| `steal` | .2 + .2 s | an attack spec: right hand low and forward, lunge 3 |\n581\t| `shove` | .06 + .08 + .3 s | both hands [3, ±3, 20] → [12, ±3, 21], lunge 4, `expr: 'angry'` |\n582\t| `knocked` | by the knockdown time | the rig's `down` 0 → 1 in .15 s, a slide, lying, getting up (the rig's own); `hurt`, `expr: 'wince'`; dizzy stars (3 small orbiting sprites) when posterized |\n583\t| `spin` | .35 s | facing + 2π; arms out; ball stays with the dribble hand |\n584\t| `defense` | loop | arms wide [3, ±8, 20], crouch, shuffling sideways |\n585\t| `block` | the jump | both arms straight up [1, ±3, 40]; `swat`: right arm [2, 3, 42] → [8, 0, 30] |\n586\t| `rebound` | the jump | both hands up [3, ±2, 40]; on the catch the ball to the chin [3, 0, 26] |\n587\t| `tipoff` | the jump | crouch, jump, right hand up [2, 2, 44] |\n588\t| `hang` | 1.2 s | both hands IK'd to two rim points (world points turned into the rig's frame each step), the body hanging below, legs swinging as a damped pendulum, then let go |\n589\t| celebrations | 1–1.4 s | chest pound (fists alternate to [3, ±1, 25]), flex (hands by the shoulders [1, ±6, 30], elbows out), raise the roof (palms pump [2, ±5, 34] ↔ [2, ±5, 42] at 3 Hz), point to the sky ([2, 3, 46]), the airplane (arms out [0, ±12, 24] while running back), robot pops, gorilla drum |\n590\t| taunts | .8 s | one per character (§10.2) |\n591\t| dunks | the flight | §10.3: hand keys over the flight's progress u, plus facing spin, flip, air tuck, legs split, slam at u ≈ .9 |\n592\t\n593\tEvery action has anticipation, a committed middle and a clean settle (the guide's rule); CPU shoves and steals wind up\n594\t.04 s longer than a human's so they read. Landing from a dunk calls `rig.land(1)` (a three-point landing) and\n595\t`rig.kick(-1)`; takeoff `rig.kick(1)`. Faces: `shout` on dunks and blocks, `smile` after scoring, `angry` on shoves,\n596\t`wince` when hit.\n597\t\n598\t### 7.4 Dressing the rigs\n599\t\n600\t`dressPlayer(spec)` → `new E.Humanoid({ size, build, weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'none', hair, hat, shorts:\n601\t{ len: .55, sock, sockLen: .35 }, colors: { skin, hair, cloth: jersey, trim, pants: shorts, boot: sneaker, glove:\n602\twristband, belt: shorts }, ...proportions })`. Jersey numbers (one digit or two in the 3×5 font, in the trim color) are\n603\tdrawn over the chest or back when that side faces the camera (project `rig.worldOffset(J.shC)` lowered by 4).\n604\tSunglasses for PIXEL: a 3×1 dark bar at the eyes from `rig.head()`. Big heads: `rig.o.headR × 1.9`.\n605\t\n606\t### 7.5 Checking motion\n607\t\n608\t`#animlab` plays any clip or dunk on any player at .25×, 1× or frame by frame, with `rig.debug(r)`; check every dunk and\n609\tcelebration with `handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs` (wind-up, strike, settle; no backward sweeps, no popping).\n610\t\n611\t---\n612\t\n613\t## 8. CPU AI (`34-ai.js`)\n614\t\n615\tEach CPU player has a brain that decides at 10 Hz (staggered per player) and steers every step, writing the same `Cmd` a\n616\thuman's controls would. Roles per possession: HANDLER, OFFBALL, DEFENDER (with a mark), REBOUNDER.\n617\t\n618\t- **Handler:** scores options each decision and commits to the best for at least .3 s (no dithering):\n619\t  `dunk` (in range, turbo ≥ .15, lane roughly clear; × SLAM), `shoot` (decided chance × points; urgent under 4 s of shot\n620\t  clock; prefers PERFECT release with its timing error), `drive` (lane clear toward the rim), `pass` / `oop` (teammate\n621\t  more open, cutting, or in oop range; minus the interception risk), `spin` (a defender squarely ahead within 20, turbo ≥\n622\t  .2), `wait` (wind gust at the Pier, an eruption telegraph in its path). Steering: seek the rim, side-step defenders\n623\t  ahead within 30, keep 24 from oil slicks and lava rings; turbo when the lane is clear and the rim is more than 80 away.\n624\t- **Off the ball:** keep 70+ from the handler; spot up at a three-point wing on the far side; cut to the far block when\n625\t  the handler drives (oop setup); call for the ball when open while the handler is pressed; go for a power-up within 120\n626\t  when no defender threatens.\n627\t- **Defense:** man-to-man; marks swap when attackers cross; stand between the mark and the rim, 18–28 away (tighter on\n628\t  the handler, sagging off the other); face the handler; try a steal when adjacent from a good angle (rate by\n629\t  difficulty × aggression × SWIPE); shove the handler in the paint or a shooter rising (aggression, turbo ≥ .3); jump to\n630\t  block when the shooter rises within 40 (reaction delay and timing error by difficulty); otherwise contest with hands\n631\t  up; help on a drive when the mark is far from the ball.\n632\t- **Rebounds and loose balls:** while a shot flies, predict its landing area (short forward simulation of the ball,\n633\t  rim bounce approximated) and send the nearest one or two; box out; jump when the ball is within reach. The nearest of\n634\t  each team chases a loose ball. After a defensive rebound or a steal, push the fast break with turbo.\n635\t- **Teammate of a human:** obeys commands (`pass` = pass to me now; `shoot` = shoot now; `oop` = throw me the oop if I'm\n636\t  in range); otherwise plays its role; never steals the human's shots; feeds a human who calls when open.\n637\t- **Boss (BLAMBOTS):** the All-Star brain plus Overclock, Magnet Hands and higher shove aggression (.8); after a reboot\n638\t  they play passively for 1 s.\n639\t- **Attract/autopilot:** the same brains, with the attract director's cheats and forced actions (§13).\n640\t\n641\t**Difficulty** (Settings → CPU difficulty; Tour stops shift it, §10.5; in-between values interpolate):\n642\t\n643\t| | Rookie | Pro | All-Star | BLAM |\n644\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n645\t| decision quality (noise) | .35 | .60 | .80 | .95 |\n646\t| reaction delay (s) | .35 | .22 | .14 | .08 |\n647\t| shot release error (s, sd) | .12 | .08 | .05 | .03 |\n648\t| block timing error (s, sd) | .18 | .12 | .07 | .04 |\n649\t| steal tries per second when adjacent | .6 | 1.0 | 1.4 | 1.8 |\n650\t| shove aggression | .20 | .45 | .65 | .80 |\n651\t| turbo use | .50 | .75 | .90 | 1.0 |\n652\t\n653\t**Comeback assist** (`comeback` 0.35; Settings Off/Low/Normal = 0/.2/.35): a team trailing by d ≥ 4 points from Q2 on\n654\tgets + `comeback × min(d, 15) / 15 × 0.12` shot chance, the same × .1 decision quality for its CPU players, and turbo\n655\trefill × (1 + .5 × that factor). It applies to humans and CPU alike (the arcade tradition); Tournament mode turns it off.\n656\t\n657\t---\n658\t\n659\t## 9. Camera, presentation and juice\n660\t\n661\t### 9.1 Framing\n662\t\n663\t- The camera director calls `game.focus(x, courtMidY, 0)` every step: x follows the ball (or its holder) with a lead of\n664\t  48 in the direction of play, `cam.smooth = .16`; the vertical framing is fixed so the far sideline sits about 32% down\n665\t  the screen and the near sideline about 8% above the bottom (tune `cam.offset`), leaving the top 40 px for the HUD\n666\t  strip clear of the backboards. Bounds keep the view between 60 beyond each baseline.\n667\t- Taller screens show more crowd and backdrop above; wider screens show more court. Player zoom: `camera: { zoom:\n668\t  [.8, 1.4] }` on match scenes.\n669\t- Tip-off: centred, zoom 1.15, easing out to 1 at the tap.\n670\t\n671\t### 9.2 Dunk cam and slow motion\n672\t\n673\tOn `dunkStart` (unless Settings → reduce motion): zoom to 1.25 over .25 s centred between the dunker and the rim;\n674\t`game.timeScale = dunkSlowMo` (.45) for .35 s around the apex; at the slam hit-stop .08 s, shake 4, a .06 s white flash\n675\t(the engine applies the comfort settings), then zoom back over .5 s. Shatters: bigger (hit-stop .15, time scale .3 for\n676\t.5 s). Supernova ignition: a .4 s ring burst and banner, no slow motion. Reduce motion: no zoom or slow motion, shake\n677\tand flash per the player's settings.\n678\t\n679\t### 9.3 Drawing the hoop, the ball and depth\n680\t\n681\tIn the broadcast view a backboard (a plane facing along x) would be seen edge-on, as a line. **Cheat it:** draw the\n682\tglass as a panel turned 30° about the vertical axis toward the camera (for the left hoop the board's width runs along\n683\t`(−sin 30°, cos 30°)` from (40, 144): near edge at (28, 164.8), far edge at (52, 123.2); mirror for the right), so its\n684\tface shows as a parallelogram. Collisions keep the true plane (§6.6). Draw:\n685\t- **Stanchion:** a padded base box behind the baseline (team color), a pole, an arm to the top of the board (thick\n686\t  `px.line`s in an `r.queue` at the hoop's y with a bias behind the board).\n687\t- **Glass:** `px.blend(g, .25, 'screen', ...)` pale blue fill, a white 1-px frame and the orange shooter's square;\n688\t  shattered: only jagged edge shards until the sponsor break replaces it.\n689\t- **Rim:** 16 points on the ring at z 80, split into a back half (queued at y ≈ 138) and a front half (y ≈ 150), so a\n690\t  ball at the rim's centre (y 144) sorts between them; 2 px, orange shaded with `E.tones`. A damped spring bends the\n691\t  front of the ring down up to 4 on hits and slams.\n692\t- **Net:** 10 strands from the ring to a lower ring (radius 5.5, z 66) with two knots each, zig-zag links between\n693\t  neighbours, each knot a damped spring point pushed out by the ball when inside (swish ripple) and by the Pier's wind;\n694\t  back strands queued at y 138, front strands at y 150.\n695\t- **Ball:** a 9×9 sprite with seams and a dark outline, 4 rotation frames advanced by speed; `r.shadow` under it sized by\n696\t  height (the shadow is how players read its depth); a held ball sorts with a bias toward the camera when the dribble\n697\t  hand is on the camera side. Comet trail (Supernova, fast passes): the last 8 positions as `px.ddisc` in additive blend.\n698\t- **Players:** `r.actor` with a 7-radius `r.shadow`; `xray: true` for human players so they stay findable behind the\n699\t  stanchions; Supernova players get `ghost` afterimages.\n700\t\n701\t### 9.4 Banners\n702\t\n703\t`E.font.title` at scale 3–4, popping in (scale 0 → 1.2 → 1 over .25 s, `outBack`), holding .8 s, fading .2 s, at 30%\n704\tof the screen's height; one at a time by priority: SHATTERED > SUPERNOVA > POSTERIZED > dunk name > ALLEY-OOP >\n705\tREJECTED > JACKPOT > THREE! > PICKPOCKET > ANKLES BROKEN. Colors: dunks gold/orange, threes cyan, blocks red, steals\n706\tgreen, Supernova white → violet → gold, shatter ice blue, jackpot gold, posterized magenta.\n707\t\n708\t### 9.5 Effects\n709\t\n710\t| Event | Recipe |\n711\t|---|---|\n712\t| dunk slam | hit-stop .08, shake 4, flash .06, `particles.ring` at the rim (4 → 26, '#fff6c0'), 16 sparks, 10 glints, crowd flashes, rumble .6 for .2 s |\n713\t| landing from a dunk | 12 dust, `rig.land(1)` |\n714\t| shatter | hit-stop .15, flash, 60 glass `bits`, 30 glints, a ring, slow motion, rumble 1 for .4 s |\n715\t| block | `particles.impact` at the ball, 8 sparks, shake 2, rumble .4 |\n716\t| steal | 6 green glints, a whoosh |\n717\t| shove hit | `particles.impact` at the contact, dust where the victim lands, shake 2 |\n718\t| swish | net ripple, 6 white glints |\n719\t| rim clank | 3 orange sparks, rim bend |\n720\t| Supernova | a violet-gold ring, 20 fire around the player, embers trailing while it lasts |\n721\t| power-up | spawn: a glint spiral and ring; pickup: 12 glints and `particles.text('+ROCKET KICKS')` |\n722\t| lava bomb | a pulsing red ring decal for 1.2 s, then `particles.explosion(x, y, 0, 1.4)`, fire, smoke |\n723\t\n724\t### 9.6 Crowd and lighting\n725\t\n726\tThe crowd: two people per stand tile on four tiers (about 370), each a small sprite (head and body, shirt colors from\n727\tthe court's palette) with its own bobbing phase, drawn one `r.queue` per row. Reactions: dunks and shatters make the\n728\tcrowd jump with arms up and pop camera flashes (white emissive dots for .6 s); a home miss slumps them; Supernova makes\n729\tthem bob on the beat (`audio.onBeat`); the Dome adds an upper deck. Every court sets `game.lights.enabled = true`, its\n730\tambient and its lights each draw (§10.1); canvas lighting only (it looks the same in every browser and check).\n731\t\n732\t---\n733\t\n734\t## 10. Content\n735\t\n736\t### 10.1 Courts\n737\t\n738\t| Court | Home of | Setting | Floor | Twist | Song |\n739\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n740\t| THE SKYBOX | Hightops | a Neon Heights rooftop at night | dark asphalt, neon magenta and cyan lines, a winged-sneaker logo | Jackpot Spot | `skybox` |\n741\t| THE PIER | Breakers | a boardwalk at sunset | weathered planks, worn white lines, a wave logo | Sea breeze (wind) | `pier` |\n742\t| THE SCRAPYARD | Crushers | a junkyard at dusk in light rain | cracked concrete, oil stains, hazard-stripe lines, a crossed-wrenches logo | Oil slicks | `scrapyard` |\n743\t| THE CALDERA | Magma | Kaboom Island's volcano at night, falling ash | basalt tiles with glowing seams, gold lines, a volcano logo | Eruptions and steam vents | `caldera` |\n744\t| THE BLAM DOME | Blambots | the championship arena | polished maple, red and gold lines, the GLOBO-BLAM logo, \"BLAM DOME\" in the keys | Boss mechanics, pyro | `dome` |\n745\t\n746\tEach court is a data entry: `{ id, name, palette, floor(x, y, tag) painter, lines colors, logo sprite, standsFace,\n747\tbackdrop spec, silhouettes(r), props [[id, x, y, opts]], crowd palette, lights(r), ambient, weather, dribbleSound,\n748\tmusic, twist }`. Floors are painted by `floorTex` like `kits/sports.js`'s pitch: analytic court lines (§6.1) plus logo\n749\tmasks (string sprites scaled ×4 into the floor's centre and keys) and the material's grain (`E.hash2`, `E.noise2`).\n750\tNew shapes (data, per `docs/ASSETS.md`, checked with `asset-sheet.mjs`): `fence-chain`, `water-tower`, `ac-unit`,\n751\t`boombox`, `beach-umbrella`, `lifeguard-tower`, `surfboard`, `junk-car` (5 colors), `tire-stack`, `tiki-totem`,\n752\t`pyro-cannon`, `tv-camera`, `scorer-table`, `trophy`, `anchor-desk`. Engine props reused: streetlamp, trashcan, palm,\n753\tawning, lantern, firedrum, barrel, torch, banner, bench, sign.\n754\t\n755\t**THE SKYBOX.** Sky `['#07061a', '#1d1240', '#3a1a5a']`, 60 stars, a moon; `city` layers (far `#140c2a` parallax .08,\n756\tnear `#1e1236` parallax .2). Silhouettes: a water tower; a \"BLAM COLA\" neon billboard that flickers; a helicopter that\n757\tcrosses every 40 s with a searchlight (a moving light and cone). Props: chain-link fence on the far apron, AC units, a\n758\tboombox on the bench, trashcans, streetlamps, neon tubes on the stands. Crowd: city kids in hoodies (magenta, cyan,\n759\tblack, yellow). Lights: ambient .45; four warm floodlights at the corners (z 140, radius 260); magenta and cyan glows at\n760\tthe signs. Dribble: a sharp asphalt slap. **Twist: Jackpot Spot** (§6.15), always on here.\n761\t\n762\t**THE PIER.** Sunset `['#2a1a4a', '#ff7a5c', '#ffd27a']`, a low sun, `sea` and `clouds` layers. Silhouettes: a turning\n763\tFerris wheel, a roller coaster whose car loops every 12 s, a lighthouse. Props: palms, beach umbrellas, a lifeguard\n764\ttower, surfboards in the sand, a cotton-candy awning, string lights (lanterns, `anchor: 'top'`). Crowd: beachgoers in\n765\tbright swimwear and sun hats. Gulls (Blobs with wings) cross overhead; one perches on a backboard and flaps off when the\n766\tball hits the glass. Lights: ambient .8, warm. Dribble: a hollow wooden thunk. **Twist: Sea breeze.** Every 15–25 s\n767\t(× `hazardInterval`) a gust blows for 4 s: wind w in −1..1, mostly along x (±25°), ball acceleration `w × 140` while\n768\tairborne, its effect on the shot chance in §6.7. A windsock at the bottom left shows direction and 1–3 chevrons; sand\n769\tand leaves stream; the net and the palms sway. The CPU waits out strong gusts unless the shot clock is short.\n770\t\n771\t**THE SCRAPYARD.** Dusk `['#120e1a', '#4a2e36', '#b0603a']`, `mountains` as junk piles, dark clouds, rain .4. Silhouettes:\n772\ta crane with a swinging magnet that drops a car with a crash at each quarter break; car stacks. Props: junk cars, tire\n773\tstacks, oil drums (barrels recolored), fire drums (`light: true`), chain-link fence, the junkyard dog (a Blob with ears,\n774\ttail and feet) on the east apron, barking at dunks. Crowd: mechanics in overalls and hard hats. Lights: ambient .6, fire\n775\tdrums, two white work lights. Dribble: a dull concrete thud. **Twist: Oil slicks.** At each quarter start, three slicks\n776\t(ellipses, radius 20–36) are placed by `S.rng` on the court away from the centre circle and the keys. On a slick a\n777\tplayer's acceleration is × .15 (it slides); turning more than 90° on a slick at turbo speed slips it with chance .3 (a\n778\t.6 s knockdown, a fumble). Slicks are glossy dark decals with a moving rainbow sheen. The CPU avoids them on turbo.\n779\t\n780\t**THE CALDERA.** Night `['#0c0408', '#3a0c10', '#7a1e10']`, a big volcano cone (`mountains`) with a glowing crater\n781\t(emissive glow, embers and smoke rising), the sea at the horizon, ash .3. Beyond the arena walls a lava moat (bright\n782\tfloor, flickering red lights and drawn bubbles). Props: tiki torches (lit), tiki totems, palms, drums; bamboo stands\n783\t(`face: 'plank'`). Crowd: islanders with flower leis. Lights: ambient .4, torches, the moat's red glow, the crater.\n784\tDribble: a stone click. **Twist: Eruptions and steam vents.** Every 25–35 s: a rumble (shake 1.5 for 1.2 s, an\n785\t\"ERUPTION!\" banner, a falling whistle), then 3 lava bombs over 3 s at spots telegraphed 1.2 s ahead by pulsing red rings\n786\t(radius 22; one near the ball, two random): anyone inside at impact is knocked down .8 s and fumbles. **Steam vents** at\n787\tcourt-local (200, 60) and (440, 228) puff for 2 s every 5 s (a visible column first): a ball handler on a puffing vent\n788\tin its offensive half pressing shoot with turbo is launched into the VOLCANO LAUNCH dunk; a defender on a puffing vent\n789\tpressing shoot jumps a SUPER BLOCK (jump × 1.6).\n790\t\n791\t**THE BLAM DOME.** Indoors: a dark arena bowl with rafters, an upper deck of crowd (6 tiers), a jumbotron hanging over\n792\tcentre court (a big screen showing the last scorer's live portrait, \"BLAM!\" and the score, and the Commissioner at story\n793\tmoments), championship banners in the teams' colors, sweeping laser lines. Props: pyro cannons at the corners, TV\n794\tcameras, the scorer's table, benches, the Golden Blamboozle trophy (a golden ball on a column) at the table. Crowd: huge,\n795\tmixed colors, foam fingers. Lights: ambient .7, six sweeping spotlights (moving lights with cones), pyro flashes.\n796\tDribble: hardwood bounce with squeaks. **Twist: the boss** (only against the BLAMBOTS): **OVERCLOCK** at the start of\n797\tQ4, and in Q3 whenever the bots trail by 8 or more: both bots go Supernova for 30 s (red visor glow, steam from their\n798\tbacks, the `overclock` music layer); **MAGNET HANDS**: bots' steal chance × 1.15, with visible blue sparks; **SYSTEM\n799\tREBOOT**: a bot knocked down twice within 10 s short-circuits for 3 s (sparks, frozen, \"SYSTEM REBOOT!\"), which is how\n800\tthe player answers the Overclock. Pyro columns fire on every score (cosmetic, with light flashes).\n801\t\n802\t### 10.2 Teams and players\n803\t\n804\tRatings in the order ZOOM / SPLASH / DEEP / SLAM / DIME / SWIPE / SWAT / BUMP.\n805\t\n806\t| Team | Colors (jersey / trim / shorts) | Logo | Style |\n807\t|---|---|---|---|\n808\t| NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS | `#ff3ca6` / `#2de2ff` / `#1a1420` | a winged sneaker | flashy, fast, high-flying |\n809\t| BOARDWALK BREAKERS | `#18c8b8` / `#ff7a5c` / `#f2d8a0` | a breaking wave | passing and threes |\n810\t| SCRAPYARD CRUSHERS | `#d8641e` / `#ffd23a` / `#1c1a18` | crossed wrenches | power and steals |\n811\t| KABOOM MAGMA | `#ff3a1a` / `#ffb020` / `#22181e` | a volcano erupting a basketball | defense and clutch shooting |\n812\t| THE BLAMBOTS (boss; unlocked by the Tour) | `#c8d0dc` / `#e8c040` / `#3a4250` | a robot fist holding a ball | everything, loudly |\n813\t| CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS (secret; unlocked by the Tour) | `#f4f0ea` / `#ffc83a` / `#4a2a8a` | the Channel BLAM microphone | showbiz |\n814\t\n815\t| Player | Team | Role | Build, size | Look | Ratings | Voice | Taunt |\n816\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n817\t| VOLT | Hightops | high-flyer | heroic 1.65 | electric-blue ponytail, magenta band, skin `#8a5a3c` | 9 5 4 9 6 6 4 3 | bright, quick, 220 Hz | raise the roof |\n818\t| BIG RUMBLE | Hightops | enforcer | bulky 1.9 | black flattop, cyan wristbands, skin `#4a2c1e` | 3 3 1 7 4 4 9 10 | deep, slow, 85 Hz | flex |\n819\t| PIXEL | Hightops | sharpshooter | heroic 1.55 | green spiky hair, shades, skin `#f0c8a0` | 6 9 9 3 7 5 3 3 | squeaky, 270 Hz | finger guns |\n820\t| RIPTIDE | Breakers | point guard | heroic 1.6 | long sun-bleached hair, skin `#d8a070` | 10 6 6 5 10 7 2 3 | laid-back drawl, 170 Hz | surf balance |\n821\t| SHELLSHOCK | Breakers | three-point bomber | heroic 1.65 | coral afro, skin `#6a4028` | 6 8 10 3 6 5 3 4 | sing-song, 200 Hz | goggles (hands circle the eyes) |\n822\t| LONGBOARD | Breakers | shot blocker | heroic 1.85, legs × 1.12 | bald, teal band, skin `#c89070` | 4 5 2 7 4 3 9 7 | slow, 120 Hz | finger wag |\n823\t| TORQUE | Crushers | power dunker | bulky 1.85 | black mohawk, skin `#c8a080` | 6 4 2 10 4 4 6 9 | gravel, 95 Hz (noise in it) | chest pound |\n824\t| SPARKPLUG | Crushers | pickpocket | chibi 1.65 | yellow cap, skin `#3a2418` | 9 6 6 4 7 10 2 2 | fast, 300 Hz | shimmy |\n825\t| HUBCAP | Crushers | veteran all-rounder | heroic 1.7 | short grey hair, skin `#e0b090` | 5 7 6 6 6 6 6 6 | grumpy, 130 Hz | taps an imaginary watch |\n826\t| OBSIDIAN | Magma | rim protector | bulky 1.95 | bald, skin `#3a2216` | 4 4 1 8 3 4 10 8 | rumbling, 78 Hz | arms crossed, stone face |\n827\t| EMBER | Magma | clutch shooter | heroic 1.6 | long red hair, skin `#f0c090` | 7 9 8 5 6 6 3 3 | crisp, 230 Hz | blows on fingertips |\n828\t| PUMICE | Magma | leaper | heroic 1.65 | black afro, skin `#8a5030` | 8 5 3 9 5 5 7 3 | bouncy, 190 Hz | pogo hops |\n829\t| DUNKATRON | Blambots | destroyer | bulky 1.95, chrome helmet, red eye glow | chrome body, gold trim | 8 6 4 10 6 8 8 8 | robot, 95 Hz | robot dance |\n830\t| SWATBOT | Blambots | wall | bulky 1.95, same | chrome, red visor | 6 7 7 7 7 9 10 9 | robot, 120 Hz | \"processing\" head tilt |\n831\t| SPARE PARTS | Blambots | bench unit | bulky 1.8, same | mismatched panels | 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 | glitchy robot, 150 Hz | glitch wave |\n832\t| VINNIE VOX | All-Stars | play-by-play man | heroic 1.7 | headset band, skin `#e8b890` | 5 7 7 5 8 5 4 5 | the announcer (low) | mic drop |\n833\t| DEE DEE DECIBEL | All-Stars | color commentator | heroic 1.6 | purple ponytail, skin `#6a4030` | 7 8 6 6 7 6 5 4 | the announcer (high) | points at the camera |\n834\t| BLAMMO | All-Stars | the league's gorilla mascot | bulky 2.0, hunch .2 | dark fur (skin and hair `#3a2e2a`), lighter face | 7 3 1 10 3 6 9 10 | gorilla | chest drum |\n835\t\n836\tStory characters (not playable): **COMMISSIONER GIGAWATT** (CEO of GLOBO-BLAM Corp; heroic 1.6, purple coat, gold belt,\n837\twhite hair, a smug smile; a nasal, slow voice), **REF ROSCOE** (referee; white shirt with black trim, black cap, a\n838\twhistle; tosses the tip-off), **INTERN 1 and INTERN 2** (Blam Camp partners in grey practice jerseys), the **cleaning\n839\tbot** (a small metal Blob that replaces shattered glass). Vinnie and Dee Dee also appear at the studio desk in suits\n840\t(`outfit: 'coat'`). Every line about a player uses the player's NAME, never a pronoun, so any line fits any player.\n841\t\n842\t### 10.3 Dunk catalog (`06-data-moves.js`)\n843\t\n844\t| Id | Banner | Needs | Distance from rim | Choreography (u = flight progress) | Style bonus |\n845\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n846\t| `hammer` | TWO-HAND HAMMER | any | 0–70 | both hands raise the ball overhead from takeoff; slam at u .9 | 0 |\n847\t| `tomahawk` | TOMAHAWK! | SLAM 5 | 30–130 | ball in the right hand cocked far behind the head (u .3–.7), whipped forward at .88 | 50 |\n848\t| `doublepump` | DOUBLE PUMP! | SLAM 6 | 30–120 | ball pumped to the waist and back up twice (u .3, .55) | 80 |\n849\t| `reverse` | REVERSE ROCKET! | SLAM 6, approach within 50° of the baseline | 20–100 | turns its back to the rim mid-flight, slams backward over the head | 100 |\n850\t| `windmill` | WINDMILL! | SLAM 7 | 50–150 | right arm circles once (down past the hip, back, over the top) | 100 |\n851\t| `threesixty` | THREE-SIXTY! | SLAM 7 | 40–140 | facing turns 2π over u .2–.85; two-hand slam | 120 |\n852\t| `ftflyer` | FREE-THROW FLYER! | SLAM 8 | 110 to the dunk range | a long glide (apex + 30), legs split, one-hand slam | 150 |\n853\t| `flip` | FRONT-FLIP FREAK! | SLAM 8 | 60–150 | `flip` 0 → 1 over u .25–.75 (a front somersault), two-hand slam | 180 |\n854\t| `rattler` | RIM RATTLER! | SLAM 4 | 0–60 | two-hand slam, then `hang` 1.2 s with legs swinging | 60 |\n855\t| `nova720` | SEVEN-TWENTY SUPERNOVA! | Supernova | 60–190 | facing turns 4π, star-fire trail | 250 |\n856\t| `volcano` | VOLCANO LAUNCH! | a steam vent | from the vent | launched (apex 160), a 2π spin, a fireball slam; shatters 20% | 300 |\n857\t| `quake` | BLAM-QUAKE!!! | overclocked BLAMBOT; Moon Shoes 50%; Supernova 15% | 80 to the dunk range | huge apex, both hands, always shatters, the landing's shockwave knocks down everyone within 40 | 400 |\n858\t\n859\tChoice: every dunk whose needs pass, weighted by its bonus and by (SLAM − its minimum + 1), drawn with `S.rng`; the\n860\tsame for humans and the CPU. Each has an announcer line family (power, spin, flip, hang, long, nova, volcano, quake).\n861\t\n862\t### 10.4 Power-up icons\n863\t\n864\t12×12 string sprites, drawn bobbing above a pulsing floor ring in their color: ROCKET KICKS (a sneaker with a flame),\n865\tGLUE GLOVES (a green dripping glove), LASER SIGHT (a red crosshair), MOON SHOES (a spring shoe), BLAM BOMB (a black bomb\n866\twith a lit fuse), GOLD BALL (a gold ball with a shine). The same icons show on the players' plates with a countdown.\n867\t\n868\t### 10.5 The Blam Tour\n869\t\n870\tPROLOGUE → STOP 1 → STOP 2 → STOP 3 → THE REVEAL → THE FINAL → ENDING → CREDITS → HALL OF BLAM ENTRY.\n871\t\n872\t| You pick | Stop 1 | Stop 2 | Stop 3 | Final |\n873\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n874\t| Hightops | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n875\t| Breakers | Hightops at the Skybox | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n876\t| Crushers | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n877\t| Magma | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n878\t\n879\t- CPU difficulty: the Settings value (default Pro) shifted by stop: stop 1 one step lower, stop 2 as set, stop 3 half a\n880\t  step higher, the final one step higher (clamped to BLAM).\n881\t- Power-ups off at stop 1, on from stop 2. Quarters 1:30. One or two players (a second human joins on the same team at\n882\t  the Tour's team select).\n883\t- Each stop: tour map → matchup card (codes) → pre-game talk → tip-off → the game → results → post-game beat → map\n884\t  (autosave). A loss: results → REMATCH? 10-second countdown (Rematch, Tour Map, Quit Tour); a rematch replays the stop.\n885\t- Tour score = the stops' style points (wins only). At the end, or on quitting after a loss, a qualifying score enters\n886\t  the Hall of Blam (`E.Arcade` initials wheel).\n887\t\n888\t### 10.6 Story script (`04-data-story.js`)\n889\t\n890\tTone: a loud 90s sports broadcast. Announcers speak in ALL CAPS, punchy, pun-heavy; the Commissioner is smug and speaks\n891\tin sentence case; robots speak in SPACED. CAPITAL. WORDS. `{TEAM}` is your team's name; `{CAPTAIN}` your first player.\n892\tBeats play in engine scenes (§11.3) as `E.Dialog` lines with live portraits and voices, staged with posed rigs and camera\n893\tmoves (`game.script`, `game.tween`). Hold confirm 1 s to skip a beat, Start to skip all of it.\n894\t\n895\t1. **prologue** (the Channel BLAM studio desk; the Commissioner on a monitor)\n896\t   - VINNIE: \"GOOD EVENING, BALL FANS! LIVE FROM THE TOP OF THE WORLD, THIS IS CHANNEL BLAM!\"\n897\t   - DEE DEE: \"AND THIS IS THE BLAM TOUR! FIVE COURTS! FOUR CREWS! ONE GOLDEN BLAMBOOZLE! ZERO FOULS!\"\n898\t   - VINNIE: \"TONIGHT'S TOUR IS SPONSORED BY GLOBO-BLAM CORP. THEY MAKE EVERYTHING. THEY MADE THIS SENTENCE.\"\n899\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Greetings, little ballers. Win my Tour and the Golden Blamboozle is yours.\"\n900\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Lose, and your court becomes a GLOBO-BLAM parking lot. Validated parking, of course. Ha. Ha. Ha.\"\n901\t   - DEE DEE: \"{TEAM}, THE WHOLE CITY IS WATCHING. NO PRESSURE! EXCEPT ALL OF IT!\"\n902\t2. **camp-offer** (first Tour only) — DEE DEE: \"FIRST TIME ON THE TOUR? HIT BLAM CAMP AND I'LL SHOW YOU THE ROPES. OR\n903\t   DON'T. LIVE DANGEROUSLY!\" Choices: BLAM CAMP / LET'S PLAY.\n904\t3. **stop intro** (each stop, at the court) — VINNIE: \"STOP {N} OF THE BLAM TOUR: {HOME} VERSUS {AWAY} AT {COURT}!\" plus\n905\t   DEE DEE's court line: Skybox \"THIRTY STORIES UP AND THE NETS ARE STILL SMOKING!\"; Pier \"WATCH THE WIND, FOLKS. AND THE\n906\t   SEAGULLS. MOSTLY THE SEAGULLS.\"; Scrapyard \"OIL ON THE FLOOR AND FIRE IN THEIR EYES!\"; Caldera \"THE FLOOR IS HOT, THE\n907\t   VOLCANO IS HOTTER, AND THE MUSIC IS HOTTEST!\"; Dome \"THE BLAM DOME! SIXTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE VERY NERVOUS\n908\t   JUMBOTRON!\"\n909\t4. **pre-game talk** (the rival captain, then your captain's reply by team):\n910\t   - vs Breakers — RIPTIDE: \"Hope you packed sunscreen, {TEAM}. The tide's coming in, and it doesn't knock.\" Replies:\n911\t     VOLT \"Cute pier. I'm about to dunk on it.\" · TORQUE \"I've crushed bigger boats than this.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Sand turns\n912\t     to glass when I'm around.\"\n913\t   - vs Hightops — VOLT: \"Welcome to the Skybox. Try not to look down. Actually, look down: that's where you'll be.\"\n914\t     Replies: RIPTIDE \"Whoa, relax. We're just here to ride the wave. Over you.\" · TORQUE \"Fancy lights. They'll look\n915\t     great on my scrap pile.\" · EMBER \"Neon's cute. Lava's hotter.\"\n916\t   - vs Crushers — TORQUE: \"We crush cars for breakfast. You look like a light snack.\" Replies: VOLT \"Then you're about\n917\t     to get a stomachache.\" · SHELLSHOCK \"Careful, the floor's greasier than your jokes.\" · PUMICE \"I bounce. You crush.\n918\t     Let's see who's still standing.\"\n919\t   - vs Magma — OBSIDIAN: \"On Kaboom Island the floor is lava. Not a game. Actual lava. Walk carefully.\" Replies:\n920\t     BIG RUMBLE \"I don't walk carefully. I walk LOUD.\" · RIPTIDE \"Dude. Is that, like, safe?\" · SPARKPLUG \"I'm too fast\n921\t     to get burned!\"\n922\t5. **post-game, stop 1** — the beaten captain: RIPTIDE \"Wipeout. Totally gnarly, though. Respect.\" · VOLT \"Okay, okay.\n923\t   You can ball. Don't let it go to your head.\" · TORQUE \"You crushed us. That's MY job.\" · OBSIDIAN \"The mountain...\n924\t   respects you.\" Then GIGAWATT (monitor): \"Hmm. Promising. My engineers are taking notes. Lots of notes.\"\n925\t6. **post-game, stop 2** — GIGAWATT: \"Data received. Prototype calibration at ninety-eight percent. Keep playing,\n926\t   little ballers. Keep... teaching them.\" DEE DEE: \"TEACHING WHO? VINNIE, WHY DOES THE GLOBO-BLAM LOGO HAVE A ROBOT\n927\t   ARM?\" VINNIE: \"THAT'S BRANDING, DEE DEE. WE DON'T ASK QUESTIONS ON LIVE TV.\"\n928\t7. **the reveal** (after stop 3, at the Dome, the Commissioner in person)\n929\t   - VINNIE: \"THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!\"\n930\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Congratulations. You have earned the privilege... of being replaced.\"\n931\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Behold the future of basketball: the BLAMBOTS! No salaries! No sweat! No mercy!\"\n932\t   - DUNKATRON: \"BEEP. YOUR. CAREER. IS. DEPRECATED.\"\n933\t   - SWATBOT: \"INITIATING. TRASH. TALK. PROTOCOL. ... YOU. STINK.\"\n934\t   - {CAPTAIN} by team: VOLT \"Did the toaster just trash-talk me?\" · RIPTIDE \"Bummer. I was gonna say we could be\n935\t     friends.\" · TORQUE \"I've got a crusher with your names on it.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Metal melts.\"\n936\t8. **final pre-game** — VINNIE: \"THE FINAL! HUMANS VERSUS HARDWARE! THE BLAMBOOZLE IS ON THE LINE!\"\n937\t9. **overclock** (in play, captions and the jumbotron) — GIGAWATT: \"OVERCLOCK THEM! MAXIMUM BLAM!\" DEE DEE: \"THE ROBOTS\n938\t   ARE GLOWING! IS THAT LEGAL? THERE ARE NO RULES! I FORGOT!\"\n939\t10. **first reboot** (in play, once) — DEE DEE: \"THEY SHORT-CIRCUIT WHEN YOU KNOCK THEM DOWN! KEEP SHOVING, {TEAM}!\"\n940\t11. **ending** (after winning the final)\n941\t    - DUNKATRON: \"ERROR. ERROR. HUMANS. TOO. ... BLAM.\" (sparks; both bots topple)\n942\t    - VINNIE: \"THEY DID IT! {TEAM} WINS THE BLAM TOUR!\"\n943\t    - DEE DEE: \"AND THE BLAMBOTS ARE BEING RECYCLED INTO VERY SAD TOASTERS!\"\n944\t    - GIGAWATT: \"This isn't over! I'll buy another league! I'll buy the MOON! Hey! Put me down!\" (BLAMMO carries the\n945\t      Commissioner off over a shoulder)\n946\t    - VINNIE: \"STREETBALL IS SAVED! THE BLAMBOOZLE GOES HOME WITH {TEAM}!\"\n947\t    - DEE DEE: \"GOODNIGHT, EVERYBODY! REMEMBER: NO FOULS! NO MERCY!\" VINNIE and DEE DEE: \"ALL BLAM!\"\n948\t12. **credits** — scrolling credits over the trophy lift and a crowd confetti storm, the `credits` song; then unlock\n949\t    cards: \"UNLOCKED: THE BLAMBOTS\", \"UNLOCKED: CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS\", \"UNLOCKED: BIG HEADS (OPTIONS)\", \"SECRETS ON\n950\t    THE ABOUT SCREEN\".\n951\t13. **losses** — stops 1–3: GIGAWATT \"Tsk. Another court for my parking empire.\" The final: GIGAWATT \"Resistance is...\n952\t    adorable.\" DUNKATRON \"GAME. OVER. INSERT. COIN.\"\n953\t14. **halftime gags** (one per halftime, no repeats within a Tour): \"THIS HALFTIME IS BROUGHT TO YOU BY GLOBO-BLAM\n954\t    SNEAKER GLUE. STICK THE LANDING. FOREVER.\" · \"OUR STATS DEPARTMENT IS ONE GUY WITH A CALCULATOR, AND HE IS\n955\t    SWEATING.\" · \"REMEMBER, KIDS: STAY IN SCHOOL. AND IN THE PAINT.\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM COLA: NOW WITH 30% MORE FIZZ AND 0%\n956\t    EXPLANATION.\" · \"IF YOU'RE JUST JOINING US: YES, THAT WAS A REAL DUNK. NO, WE DON'T KNOW HOW EITHER.\" · \"WE ASKED THE\n957\t    ROBOTS FOR A HALFTIME COMMENT. THEY SENT US A RECEIPT.\"\n958\t15. **sponsor breaks** (one per shatter) — \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK AFTER THIS MESSAGE FROM GLOBO-BLAM GLASS: NOW 40% LESS\n959\t    SHATTERY!\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM INSURANCE: BECAUSE SOMEBODY HAS TO PAY FOR THAT.\" · \"THIS REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD IS BROUGHT\n960\t    TO YOU BY... THE LAST REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD.\"\n961\t\n962\t### 10.7 Announcer lines (`05-data-lines.js`)\n963\t\n964\tBanks by event, at least 10 lines each (write them in the voice of the samples), ALL CAPS, at most 60 characters a\n965\tline, with `{NAME}`, `{VICTIM}`, `{TEAM}` slots. Rules: big plays interrupt small ones; at most two captions per\n966\tpossession; no line repeats within the last 8; per-bank cooldowns; Settings → Commentary (Full, Big plays, Off). VINNIE\n967\tcalls the play, DEE DEE adds the color; alternate them. Samples:\n968\t\n969\t| Bank | Samples |\n970\t|---|---|\n971\t| tipoff | \"WELCOME TO CHANNEL BLAM! LET'S GET LOUD!\" · \"THE BALL IS UP! THE CROWD IS UP! I AM UP!\" |\n972\t| dunk (power) | \"BLAMMO! {NAME} JUST MAILED IT FIRST CLASS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL A CARPENTER, THAT RIM IS FINISHED!\" · \"KA-BLAM! THE CROWD LEFT THEIR SEATS. AND THEIR SHOES!\" |\n973\t| dunk (spin, flip, hang, long) | \"{NAME} SPUN SO FAST THE SCOREBOARD GOT DIZZY!\" · \"A FRONT FLIP?! THAT'S NOT BASKETBALL, THAT'S THE CIRCUS!\" · \"{NAME} IS HANGING ON THAT RIM LIKE IT OWES MONEY!\" · \"AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL HAS QUESTIONS FOR {NAME}!\" |\n974\t| alley-oop | \"SPECIAL DELIVERY! SIGNED, SEALED, SLAMMED!\" |\n975\t| three / deep three | \"SPLASH! BRING A TOWEL!\" · \"THAT WAS FROM A DIFFERENT ZIP CODE!\" · \"{NAME} SHOT THAT FROM THE PARKING LOT! VALIDATED!\" |\n976\t| airball | \"AIRBALL! THE SEAGULLS SAY THANK YOU!\" · \"THAT ONE IS STILL GOING. IT'S IN ORBIT.\" |\n977\t| block | \"REJECTED! RETURN TO SENDER!\" · \"{NAME} SAYS NOT IN MY HOUSE, NOT IN MY YARD, NOT IN MY ZIP CODE!\" |\n978\t| steal | \"PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!\" · \"{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!\" |\n979\t| shove | \"NO FOULS IN BASKETBLAM, BABY!\" · \"THAT'S NOT A FOUL. THAT'S A LIFESTYLE.\" · \"{VICTIM} JUST GOT SENT TO THE SHADOW REALM!\" |\n980\t| ankles | \"ANKLES! {VICTIM} NEEDS A NEW PAIR!\" |\n981\t| posterized | \"FRAME IT! HANG IT! {VICTIM} IS ON {NAME}'S WALL NOW!\" |\n982\t| Supernova on / off | \"{NAME} HAS GONE SUPERNOVA! DIM THE LIGHTS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL NASA, {NAME} IS A STAR!\" · \"AND THE STAR COLLAPSES! BACK TO EARTH, {NAME}!\" |\n983\t| shatter | \"THE GLASS! THE GLASS IS GONE!\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A BROOM. A BIGGER BROOM!\" |\n984\t| goaltend | \"GOALTENDING! THE BUCKET COUNTS, AND SO DOES THE SHAME!\" |\n985\t| jackpot | \"JACKPOT! {NAME} HIT THE SPOT AND THE SPOT PAID OUT!\" |\n986\t| power-ups | \"ROCKET KICKS! {NAME} IS LEGALLY A VEHICLE NOW!\" · \"GLUE GLOVES! THAT BALL ISN'T GOING ANYWHERE!\" · \"LASER SIGHT! {NAME} CAN SEE THE FUTURE, AND IT'S A BUCKET!\" · \"MOON SHOES! GRAVITY HAS LEFT THE BUILDING!\" · \"BLAM BOMB! EVERYBODY DUCK!\" · \"GOLD BALL! NEXT BUCKET'S WORTH DOUBLE!\" |\n987\t| clutch / buzzer | \"TEN SECONDS! HEARTS POUNDING! SNEAKERS SQUEAKING!\" · \"AT THE BUZZER! I BROKE MY CHAIR! I NEED A NEW CHAIR!\" |\n988\t| comeback / blowout | \"{TEAM} IS CLAWING BACK! DON'T TOUCH THAT DIAL!\" · \"THIS ONE'S GETTING UGLY. I'M COVERING MY EYES. I'M PEEKING.\" |\n989\t| twists | \"BIG GUST OFF THE OCEAN! HOLD ONTO YOUR HATS AND YOUR JUMPERS!\" · \"{NAME} HIT THE OIL! THAT'S A SLIP 'N SLAM!\" · \"THE VOLCANO WANTS IN ON THE ACTION!\" · \"{NAME} RODE THE STEAM VENT TO THE MOON!\" |\n990\t| boss | \"THE ROBOTS ARE OVERCLOCKING! SMELLS LIKE BURNT TOAST IN HERE!\" · \"SYSTEM REBOOT! TURN IT OFF AND ON AGAIN, BABY!\" · \"THOSE ROBOTS RUN ON BATTERIES AND BAD MANNERS!\" |\n991\t| shot clock | \"SHOT CLOCK! YOU HAVE TO SHOOT IT EVENTUALLY, FOLKS!\" |\n992\t| quarter end / halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE QUARTER! CATCH YOUR BREATH, I CAN'T!\" · \"HALFTIME! STRETCH YOUR LEGS AND YOUR VOCABULARY!\" · \"FINAL! {TEAM} TAKES IT!\" |\n993\t\n994\tPlayers also bark short trash talk when they taunt, dunk on someone or get a steal (3–5 lines each in their own voice,\n995\te.g. VOLT \"Too slow!\", BIG RUMBLE \"Move.\", SPARKPLUG \"Mine now!\", DUNKATRON \"BALL. ACQUIRED.\").\n996\t\n997\t### 10.8 Cheat codes and unlocks"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"28c61127-4d4b-4242-95e8-069fbca092ec","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:18:43.432Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-061830__x5a4f79/work/PLAN.md","content":"| `passFlair` (behind the back; 15%, always in Supernova) | .12 s | right hand sweeps [0, 5, 14] → [−3, −4, 14] |\n| `catch` | until the ball arrives | both hands reach toward where the ball will be in .15 s |\n| `steal` | .2 + .2 s | an attack spec: right hand low and forward, lunge 3 |\n| `shove` | .06 + .08 + .3 s | both hands [3, ±3, 20] → [12, ±3, 21], lunge 4, `expr: 'angry'` |\n| `knocked` | by the knockdown time | the rig's `down` 0 → 1 in .15 s, a slide, lying, getting up (the rig's own); `hurt`, `expr: 'wince'`; dizzy stars (3 small orbiting sprites) when posterized |\n| `spin` | .35 s | facing + 2π; arms out; ball stays with the dribble hand |\n| `defense` | loop | arms wide [3, ±8, 20], crouch, shuffling sideways |\n| `block` | the jump | both arms straight up [1, ±3, 40]; `swat`: right arm [2, 3, 42] → [8, 0, 30] |\n| `rebound` | the jump | both hands up [3, ±2, 40]; on the catch the ball to the chin [3, 0, 26] |\n| `tipoff` | the jump | crouch, jump, right hand up [2, 2, 44] |\n| `hang` | 1.2 s | both hands IK'd to two rim points (world points turned into the rig's frame each step), the body hanging below, legs swinging as a damped pendulum, then let go |\n| celebrations | 1–1.4 s | chest pound (fists alternate to [3, ±1, 25]), flex (hands by the shoulders [1, ±6, 30], elbows out), raise the roof (palms pump [2, ±5, 34] ↔ [2, ±5, 42] at 3 Hz), point to the sky ([2, 3, 46]), the airplane (arms out [0, ±12, 24] while running back), robot pops, gorilla drum |\n| taunts | .8 s | one per character (§10.2) |\n| dunks | the flight | §10.3: hand keys over the flight's progress u, plus facing spin, flip, air tuck, legs split, slam at u ≈ .9 |\n\nEvery action has anticipation, a committed middle and a clean settle (the guide's rule); CPU shoves and steals wind up\n.04 s longer than a human's so they read. Landing from a dunk calls `rig.land(1)` (a three-point landing) and\n`rig.kick(-1)`; takeoff `rig.kick(1)`. Faces: `shout` on dunks and blocks, `smile` after scoring, `angry` on shoves,\n`wince` when hit.\n\n### 7.4 Dressing the rigs\n\n`dressPlayer(spec)` → `new E.Humanoid({ size, build, weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'none', hair, hat, shorts:\n{ len: .55, sock, sockLen: .35 }, colors: { skin, hair, cloth: jersey, trim, pants: shorts, boot: sneaker, glove:\nwristband, belt: shorts }, ...proportions })`. Jersey numbers (one digit or two in the 3×5 font, in the trim color) are\ndrawn over the chest or back when that side faces the camera (project `rig.worldOffset(J.shC)` lowered by 4).\nSunglasses for PIXEL: a 3×1 dark bar at the eyes from `rig.head()`. Big heads: `rig.o.headR × 1.9`.\n\n### 7.5 Checking motion\n\n`#animlab` plays any clip or dunk on any player at .25×, 1× or frame by frame, with `rig.debug(r)`; check every dunk and\ncelebration with `handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs` (wind-up, strike, settle; no backward sweeps, no popping).\n\n---\n\n## 8. CPU AI (`34-ai.js`)\n\nEach CPU player has a brain that decides at 10 Hz (staggered per player) and steers every step, writing the same `Cmd` a\nhuman's controls would. Roles per possession: HANDLER, OFFBALL, DEFENDER (with a mark), REBOUNDER.\n\n- **Handler:** scores options each decision and commits to the best for at least .3 s (no dithering):\n  `dunk` (in range, turbo ≥ .15, lane roughly clear; × SLAM), `shoot` (decided chance × points; urgent under 4 s of shot\n  clock; prefers PERFECT release with its timing error), `drive` (lane clear toward the rim), `pass` / `oop` (teammate\n  more open, cutting, or in oop range; minus the interception risk), `spin` (a defender squarely ahead within 20, turbo ≥\n  .2), `wait` (wind gust at the Pier, an eruption telegraph in its path). Steering: seek the rim, side-step defenders\n  ahead within 30, keep 24 from oil slicks and lava rings; turbo when the lane is clear and the rim is more than 80 away.\n- **Off the ball:** keep 70+ from the handler; spot up at a three-point wing on the far side; cut to the far block when\n  the handler drives (oop setup); call for the ball when open while the handler is pressed; go for a power-up within 120\n  when no defender threatens.\n- **Defense:** man-to-man; marks swap when attackers cross; stand between the mark and the rim, 18–28 away (tighter on\n  the handler, sagging off the other); face the handler; try a steal when adjacent from a good angle (rate by\n  difficulty × aggression × SWIPE); shove the handler in the paint or a shooter rising (aggression, turbo ≥ .3); jump to\n  block when the shooter rises within 40 (reaction delay and timing error by difficulty); otherwise contest with hands\n  up; help on a drive when the mark is far from the ball.\n- **Rebounds and loose balls:** while a shot flies, predict its landing area (short forward simulation of the ball,\n  rim bounce approximated) and send the nearest one or two; box out; jump when the ball is within reach. The nearest of\n  each team chases a loose ball. After a defensive rebound or a steal, push the fast break with turbo.\n- **Teammate of a human:** obeys commands (`pass` = pass to me now; `shoot` = shoot now; `oop` = throw me the oop if I'm\n  in range); otherwise plays its role; never steals the human's shots; feeds a human who calls when open.\n- **Boss (BLAMBOTS):** the All-Star brain plus Overclock, Magnet Hands and higher shove aggression (.8); after a reboot\n  they play passively for 1 s.\n- **Attract/autopilot:** the same brains, with the attract director's cheats and forced actions (§13).\n\n**Difficulty** (Settings → CPU difficulty; Tour stops shift it, §10.5; in-between values interpolate):\n\n| | Rookie | Pro | All-Star | BLAM |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| decision quality (noise) | .35 | .60 | .80 | .95 |\n| reaction delay (s) | .35 | .22 | .14 | .08 |\n| shot release error (s, sd) | .12 | .08 | .05 | .03 |\n| block timing error (s, sd) | .18 | .12 | .07 | .04 |\n| steal tries per second when adjacent | .6 | 1.0 | 1.4 | 1.8 |\n| shove aggression | .20 | .45 | .65 | .80 |\n| turbo use | .50 | .75 | .90 | 1.0 |\n\n**Comeback assist** (`comeback` 0.35; Settings Off/Low/Normal = 0/.2/.35): a team trailing by d ≥ 4 points from Q2 on\ngets + `comeback × min(d, 15) / 15 × 0.12` shot chance, the same × .1 decision quality for its CPU players, and turbo\nrefill × (1 + .5 × that factor). It applies to humans and CPU alike (the arcade tradition); Tournament mode turns it off.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Camera, presentation and juice\n\n### 9.1 Framing\n\n- The camera director calls `game.focus(x, courtMidY, 0)` every step: x follows the ball (or its holder) with a lead of\n  48 in the direction of play, `cam.smooth = .16`; the vertical framing is fixed so the far sideline sits about 32% down\n  the screen and the near sideline about 8% above the bottom (tune `cam.offset`), leaving the top 40 px for the HUD\n  strip clear of the backboards. Bounds keep the view between 60 beyond each baseline.\n- Taller screens show more crowd and backdrop above; wider screens show more court. Player zoom: `camera: { zoom:\n  [.8, 1.4] }` on match scenes.\n- Tip-off: centred, zoom 1.15, easing out to 1 at the tap.\n\n### 9.2 Dunk cam and slow motion\n\nOn `dunkStart` (unless Settings → reduce motion): zoom to 1.25 over .25 s centred between the dunker and the rim;\n`game.timeScale = dunkSlowMo` (.45) for .35 s around the apex; at the slam hit-stop .08 s, shake 4, a .06 s white flash\n(the engine applies the comfort settings), then zoom back over .5 s. Shatters: bigger (hit-stop .15, time scale .3 for\n.5 s). Supernova ignition: a .4 s ring burst and banner, no slow motion. Reduce motion: no zoom or slow motion, shake\nand flash per the player's settings.\n\n### 9.3 Drawing the hoop, the ball and depth\n\nIn the broadcast view a backboard (a plane facing along x) would be seen edge-on, as a line. **Cheat it:** draw the\nglass as a panel turned 30° about the vertical axis toward the camera (for the left hoop the board's width runs along\n`(−sin 30°, cos 30°)` from (40, 144): near edge at (28, 164.8), far edge at (52, 123.2); mirror for the right), so its\nface shows as a parallelogram. Collisions keep the true plane (§6.6). Draw:\n- **Stanchion:** a padded base box behind the baseline (team color), a pole, an arm to the top of the board (thick\n  `px.line`s in an `r.queue` at the hoop's y with a bias behind the board).\n- **Glass:** `px.blend(g, .25, 'screen', ...)` pale blue fill, a white 1-px frame and the orange shooter's square;\n  shattered: only jagged edge shards until the sponsor break replaces it.\n- **Rim:** 16 points on the ring at z 80, split into a back half (queued at y ≈ 138) and a front half (y ≈ 150), so a\n  ball at the rim's centre (y 144) sorts between them; 2 px, orange shaded with `E.tones`. A damped spring bends the\n  front of the ring down up to 4 on hits and slams.\n- **Net:** 10 strands from the ring to a lower ring (radius 5.5, z 66) with two knots each, zig-zag links between\n  neighbours, each knot a damped spring point pushed out by the ball when inside (swish ripple) and by the Pier's wind;\n  back strands queued at y 138, front strands at y 150.\n- **Ball:** a 9×9 sprite with seams and a dark outline, 4 rotation frames advanced by speed; `r.shadow` under it sized by\n  height (the shadow is how players read its depth); a held ball sorts with a bias toward the camera when the dribble\n  hand is on the camera side. Comet trail (Supernova, fast passes): the last 8 positions as `px.ddisc` in additive blend.\n- **Players:** `r.actor` with a 7-radius `r.shadow`; `xray: true` for human players so they stay findable behind the\n  stanchions; Supernova players get `ghost` afterimages.\n\n### 9.4 Banners\n\n`E.font.title` at scale 3–4, popping in (scale 0 → 1.2 → 1 over .25 s, `outBack`), holding .8 s, fading .2 s, at 30%\nof the screen's height; one at a time by priority: SHATTERED > SUPERNOVA > POSTERIZED > dunk name > ALLEY-OOP >\nREJECTED > JACKPOT > THREE! > PICKPOCKET > ANKLES BROKEN. Colors: dunks gold/orange, threes cyan, blocks red, steals\ngreen, Supernova white → violet → gold, shatter ice blue, jackpot gold, posterized magenta.\n\n### 9.5 Effects\n\n| Event | Recipe |\n|---|---|\n| dunk slam | hit-stop .08, shake 4, flash .06, `particles.ring` at the rim (4 → 26, '#fff6c0'), 16 sparks, 10 glints, crowd flashes, rumble .6 for .2 s |\n| landing from a dunk | 12 dust, `rig.land(1)` |\n| shatter | hit-stop .15, flash, 60 glass `bits`, 30 glints, a ring, slow motion, rumble 1 for .4 s |\n| block | `particles.impact` at the ball, 8 sparks, shake 2, rumble .4 |\n| steal | 6 green glints, a whoosh |\n| shove hit | `particles.impact` at the contact, dust where the victim lands, shake 2 |\n| swish | net ripple, 6 white glints |\n| rim clank | 3 orange sparks, rim bend |\n| Supernova | a violet-gold ring, 20 fire around the player, embers trailing while it lasts |\n| power-up | spawn: a glint spiral and ring; pickup: 12 glints and `particles.text('+ROCKET KICKS')` |\n| lava bomb | a pulsing red ring decal for 1.2 s, then `particles.explosion(x, y, 0, 1.4)`, fire, smoke |\n\n### 9.6 Crowd and lighting\n\nThe crowd: two people per stand tile on four tiers (about 370), each a small sprite (head and body, shirt colors from\nthe court's palette) with its own bobbing phase, drawn one `r.queue` per row. Reactions: dunks and shatters make the\ncrowd jump with arms up and pop camera flashes (white emissive dots for .6 s); a home miss slumps them; Supernova makes\nthem bob on the beat (`audio.onBeat`); the Dome adds an upper deck. Every court sets `game.lights.enabled = true`, its\nambient and its lights each draw (§10.1); canvas lighting only (it looks the same in every browser and check).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Content\n\n### 10.1 Courts\n\n| Court | Home of | Setting | Floor | Twist | Song |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| THE SKYBOX | Hightops | a Neon Heights rooftop at night | dark asphalt, neon magenta and cyan lines, a winged-sneaker logo | Jackpot Spot | `skybox` |\n| THE PIER | Breakers | a boardwalk at sunset | weathered planks, worn white lines, a wave logo | Sea breeze (wind) | `pier` |\n| THE SCRAPYARD | Crushers | a junkyard at dusk in light rain | cracked concrete, oil stains, hazard-stripe lines, a crossed-wrenches logo | Oil slicks | `scrapyard` |\n| THE CALDERA | Magma | Kaboom Island's volcano at night, falling ash | basalt tiles with glowing seams, gold lines, a volcano logo | Eruptions and steam vents | `caldera` |\n| THE BLAM DOME | Blambots | the championship arena | polished maple, red and gold lines, the GLOBO-BLAM logo, \"BLAM DOME\" in the keys | Boss mechanics, pyro | `dome` |\n\nEach court is a data entry: `{ id, name, palette, floor(x, y, tag) painter, lines colors, logo sprite, standsFace,\nbackdrop spec, silhouettes(r), props [[id, x, y, opts]], crowd palette, lights(r), ambient, weather, dribbleSound,\nmusic, twist }`. Floors are painted by `floorTex` like `kits/sports.js`'s pitch: analytic court lines (§6.1) plus logo\nmasks (string sprites scaled ×4 into the floor's centre and keys) and the material's grain (`E.hash2`, `E.noise2`).\nNew shapes (data, per `docs/ASSETS.md`, checked with `asset-sheet.mjs`): `fence-chain`, `water-tower`, `ac-unit`,\n`boombox`, `beach-umbrella`, `lifeguard-tower`, `surfboard`, `junk-car` (5 colors), `tire-stack`, `tiki-totem`,\n`pyro-cannon`, `tv-camera`, `scorer-table`, `trophy`, `anchor-desk`. Engine props reused: streetlamp, trashcan, palm,\nawning, lantern, firedrum, barrel, torch, banner, bench, sign.\n\n**THE SKYBOX.** Sky `['#07061a', '#1d1240', '#3a1a5a']`, 60 stars, a moon; `city` layers (far `#140c2a` parallax .08,\nnear `#1e1236` parallax .2). Silhouettes: a water tower; a \"BLAM COLA\" neon billboard that flickers; a helicopter that\ncrosses every 40 s with a searchlight (a moving light and cone). Props: chain-link fence on the far apron, AC units, a\nboombox on the bench, trashcans, streetlamps, neon tubes on the stands. Crowd: city kids in hoodies (magenta, cyan,\nblack, yellow). Lights: ambient .45; four warm floodlights at the corners (z 140, radius 260); magenta and cyan glows at\nthe signs. Dribble: a sharp asphalt slap. **Twist: Jackpot Spot** (§6.15), always on here.\n\n**THE PIER.** Sunset `['#2a1a4a', '#ff7a5c', '#ffd27a']`, a low sun, `sea` and `clouds` layers. Silhouettes: a turning\nFerris wheel, a roller coaster whose car loops every 12 s, a lighthouse. Props: palms, beach umbrellas, a lifeguard\ntower, surfboards in the sand, a cotton-candy awning, string lights (lanterns, `anchor: 'top'`). Crowd: beachgoers in\nbright swimwear and sun hats. Gulls (Blobs with wings) cross overhead; one perches on a backboard and flaps off when the\nball hits the glass. Lights: ambient .8, warm. Dribble: a hollow wooden thunk. **Twist: Sea breeze.** Every 15–25 s\n(× `hazardInterval`) a gust blows for 4 s: wind w in −1..1, mostly along x (±25°), ball acceleration `w × 140` while\nairborne, its effect on the shot chance in §6.7. A windsock at the bottom left shows direction and 1–3 chevrons; sand\nand leaves stream; the net and the palms sway. The CPU waits out strong gusts unless the shot clock is short.\n\n**THE SCRAPYARD.** Dusk `['#120e1a', '#4a2e36', '#b0603a']`, `mountains` as junk piles, dark clouds, rain .4. Silhouettes:\na crane with a swinging magnet that drops a car with a crash at each quarter break; car stacks. Props: junk cars, tire\nstacks, oil drums (barrels recolored), fire drums (`light: true`), chain-link fence, the junkyard dog (a Blob with ears,\ntail and feet) on the east apron, barking at dunks. Crowd: mechanics in overalls and hard hats. Lights: ambient .6, fire\ndrums, two white work lights. Dribble: a dull concrete thud. **Twist: Oil slicks.** At each quarter start, three slicks\n(ellipses, radius 20–36) are placed by `S.rng` on the court away from the centre circle and the keys. On a slick a\nplayer's acceleration is × .15 (it slides); turning more than 90° on a slick at turbo speed slips it with chance .3 (a\n.6 s knockdown, a fumble). Slicks are glossy dark decals with a moving rainbow sheen. The CPU avoids them on turbo.\n\n**THE CALDERA.** Night `['#0c0408', '#3a0c10', '#7a1e10']`, a big volcano cone (`mountains`) with a glowing crater\n(emissive glow, embers and smoke rising), the sea at the horizon, ash .3. Beyond the arena walls a lava moat (bright\nfloor, flickering red lights and drawn bubbles). Props: tiki torches (lit), tiki totems, palms, drums; bamboo stands\n(`face: 'plank'`). Crowd: islanders with flower leis. Lights: ambient .4, torches, the moat's red glow, the crater.\nDribble: a stone click. **Twist: Eruptions and steam vents.** Every 25–35 s: a rumble (shake 1.5 for 1.2 s, an\n\"ERUPTION!\" banner, a falling whistle), then 3 lava bombs over 3 s at spots telegraphed 1.2 s ahead by pulsing red rings\n(radius 22; one near the ball, two random): anyone inside at impact is knocked down .8 s and fumbles. **Steam vents** at\ncourt-local (200, 60) and (440, 228) puff for 2 s every 5 s (a visible column first): a ball handler on a puffing vent\nin its offensive half pressing shoot with turbo is launched into the VOLCANO LAUNCH dunk; a defender on a puffing vent\npressing shoot jumps a SUPER BLOCK (jump × 1.6).\n\n**THE BLAM DOME.** Indoors: a dark arena bowl with rafters, an upper deck of crowd (6 tiers), a jumbotron hanging over\ncentre court (a big screen showing the last scorer's live portrait, \"BLAM!\" and the score, and the Commissioner at story\nmoments), championship banners in the teams' colors, sweeping laser lines. Props: pyro cannons at the corners, TV\ncameras, the scorer's table, benches, the Golden Blamboozle trophy (a golden ball on a column) at the table. Crowd: huge,\nmixed colors, foam fingers. Lights: ambient .7, six sweeping spotlights (moving lights with cones), pyro flashes.\nDribble: hardwood bounce with squeaks. **Twist: the boss** (only against the BLAMBOTS): **OVERCLOCK** at the start of\nQ4, and in Q3 whenever the bots trail by 8 or more: both bots go Supernova for 30 s (red visor glow, steam from their\nbacks, the `overclock` music layer); **MAGNET HANDS**: bots' steal chance × 1.15, with visible blue sparks; **SYSTEM\nREBOOT**: a bot knocked down twice within 10 s short-circuits for 3 s (sparks, frozen, \"SYSTEM REBOOT!\"), which is how\nthe player answers the Overclock. Pyro columns fire on every score (cosmetic, with light flashes).\n\n### 10.2 Teams and players\n\nRatings in the order ZOOM / SPLASH / DEEP / SLAM / DIME / SWIPE / SWAT / BUMP.\n\n| Team | Colors (jersey / trim / shorts) | Logo | Style |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS | `#ff3ca6` / `#2de2ff` / `#1a1420` | a winged sneaker | flashy, fast, high-flying |\n| BOARDWALK BREAKERS | `#18c8b8` / `#ff7a5c` / `#f2d8a0` | a breaking wave | passing and threes |\n| SCRAPYARD CRUSHERS | `#d8641e` / `#ffd23a` / `#1c1a18` | crossed wrenches | power and steals |\n| KABOOM MAGMA | `#ff3a1a` / `#ffb020` / `#22181e` | a volcano erupting a basketball | defense and clutch shooting |\n| THE BLAMBOTS (boss; unlocked by the Tour) | `#c8d0dc` / `#e8c040` / `#3a4250` | a robot fist holding a ball | everything, loudly |\n| CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS (secret; unlocked by the Tour) | `#f4f0ea` / `#ffc83a` / `#4a2a8a` | the Channel BLAM microphone | showbiz |\n\n| Player | Team | Role | Build, size | Look | Ratings | Voice | Taunt |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VOLT | Hightops | high-flyer | heroic 1.65 | electric-blue ponytail, magenta band, skin `#8a5a3c` | 9 5 4 9 6 6 4 3 | bright, quick, 220 Hz | raise the roof |\n| BIG RUMBLE | Hightops | enforcer | bulky 1.9 | black flattop, cyan wristbands, skin `#4a2c1e` | 3 3 1 7 4 4 9 10 | deep, slow, 85 Hz | flex |\n| PIXEL | Hightops | sharpshooter | heroic 1.55 | green spiky hair, shades, skin `#f0c8a0` | 6 9 9 3 7 5 3 3 | squeaky, 270 Hz | finger guns |\n| RIPTIDE | Breakers | point guard | heroic 1.6 | long sun-bleached hair, skin `#d8a070` | 10 6 6 5 10 7 2 3 | laid-back drawl, 170 Hz | surf balance |\n| SHELLSHOCK | Breakers | three-point bomber | heroic 1.65 | coral afro, skin `#6a4028` | 6 8 10 3 6 5 3 4 | sing-song, 200 Hz | goggles (hands circle the eyes) |\n| LONGBOARD | Breakers | shot blocker | heroic 1.85, legs × 1.12 | bald, teal band, skin `#c89070` | 4 5 2 7 4 3 9 7 | slow, 120 Hz | finger wag |\n| TORQUE | Crushers | power dunker | bulky 1.85 | black mohawk, skin `#c8a080` | 6 4 2 10 4 4 6 9 | gravel, 95 Hz (noise in it) | chest pound |\n| SPARKPLUG | Crushers | pickpocket | chibi 1.65 | yellow cap, skin `#3a2418` | 9 6 6 4 7 10 2 2 | fast, 300 Hz | shimmy |\n| HUBCAP | Crushers | veteran all-rounder | heroic 1.7 | short grey hair, skin `#e0b090` | 5 7 6 6 6 6 6 6 | grumpy, 130 Hz | taps an imaginary watch |\n| OBSIDIAN | Magma | rim protector | bulky 1.95 | bald, skin `#3a2216` | 4 4 1 8 3 4 10 8 | rumbling, 78 Hz | arms crossed, stone face |\n| EMBER | Magma | clutch shooter | heroic 1.6 | long red hair, skin `#f0c090` | 7 9 8 5 6 6 3 3 | crisp, 230 Hz | blows on fingertips |\n| PUMICE | Magma | leaper | heroic 1.65 | black afro, skin `#8a5030` | 8 5 3 9 5 5 7 3 | bouncy, 190 Hz | pogo hops |\n| DUNKATRON | Blambots | destroyer | bulky 1.95, chrome helmet, red eye glow | chrome body, gold trim | 8 6 4 10 6 8 8 8 | robot, 95 Hz | robot dance |\n| SWATBOT | Blambots | wall | bulky 1.95, same | chrome, red visor | 6 7 7 7 7 9 10 9 | robot, 120 Hz | \"processing\" head tilt |\n| SPARE PARTS | Blambots | bench unit | bulky 1.8, same | mismatched panels | 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 | glitchy robot, 150 Hz | glitch wave |\n| VINNIE VOX | All-Stars | play-by-play man | heroic 1.7 | headset band, skin `#e8b890` | 5 7 7 5 8 5 4 5 | the announcer (low) | mic drop |\n| DEE DEE DECIBEL | All-Stars | color commentator | heroic 1.6 | purple ponytail, skin `#6a4030` | 7 8 6 6 7 6 5 4 | the announcer (high) | points at the camera |\n| BLAMMO | All-Stars | the league's gorilla mascot | bulky 2.0, hunch .2 | dark fur (skin and hair `#3a2e2a`), lighter face | 7 3 1 10 3 6 9 10 | gorilla | chest drum |\n\nStory characters (not playable): **COMMISSIONER GIGAWATT** (CEO of GLOBO-BLAM Corp; heroic 1.6, purple coat, gold belt,\nwhite hair, a smug smile; a nasal, slow voice), **REF ROSCOE** (referee; white shirt with black trim, black cap, a\nwhistle; tosses the tip-off), **INTERN 1 and INTERN 2** (Blam Camp partners in grey practice jerseys), the **cleaning\nbot** (a small metal Blob that replaces shattered glass). Vinnie and Dee Dee also appear at the studio desk in suits\n(`outfit: 'coat'`). Every line about a player uses the player's NAME, never a pronoun, so any line fits any player.\n\n### 10.3 Dunk catalog (`06-data-moves.js`)\n\n| Id | Banner | Needs | Distance from rim | Choreography (u = flight progress) | Style bonus |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `hammer` | TWO-HAND HAMMER | any | 0–70 | both hands raise the ball overhead from takeoff; slam at u .9 | 0 |\n| `tomahawk` | TOMAHAWK! | SLAM 5 | 30–130 | ball in the right hand cocked far behind the head (u .3–.7), whipped forward at .88 | 50 |\n| `doublepump` | DOUBLE PUMP! | SLAM 6 | 30–120 | ball pumped to the waist and back up twice (u .3, .55) | 80 |\n| `reverse` | REVERSE ROCKET! | SLAM 6, approach within 50° of the baseline | 20–100 | turns its back to the rim mid-flight, slams backward over the head | 100 |\n| `windmill` | WINDMILL! | SLAM 7 | 50–150 | right arm circles once (down past the hip, back, over the top) | 100 |\n| `threesixty` | THREE-SIXTY! | SLAM 7 | 40–140 | facing turns 2π over u .2–.85; two-hand slam | 120 |\n| `ftflyer` | FREE-THROW FLYER! | SLAM 8 | 110 to the dunk range | a long glide (apex + 30), legs split, one-hand slam | 150 |\n| `flip` | FRONT-FLIP FREAK! | SLAM 8 | 60–150 | `flip` 0 → 1 over u .25–.75 (a front somersault), two-hand slam | 180 |\n| `rattler` | RIM RATTLER! | SLAM 4 | 0–60 | two-hand slam, then `hang` 1.2 s with legs swinging | 60 |\n| `nova720` | SEVEN-TWENTY SUPERNOVA! | Supernova | 60–190 | facing turns 4π, star-fire trail | 250 |\n| `volcano` | VOLCANO LAUNCH! | a steam vent | from the vent | launched (apex 160), a 2π spin, a fireball slam; shatters 20% | 300 |\n| `quake` | BLAM-QUAKE!!! | overclocked BLAMBOT; Moon Shoes 50%; Supernova 15% | 80 to the dunk range | huge apex, both hands, always shatters, the landing's shockwave knocks down everyone within 40 | 400 |\n\nChoice: every dunk whose needs pass, weighted by its bonus and by (SLAM − its minimum + 1), drawn with `S.rng`; the\nsame for humans and the CPU. Each has an announcer line family (power, spin, flip, hang, long, nova, volcano, quake).\n\n### 10.4 Power-up icons\n\n12×12 string sprites, drawn bobbing above a pulsing floor ring in their color: ROCKET KICKS (a sneaker with a flame),\nGLUE GLOVES (a green dripping glove), LASER SIGHT (a red crosshair), MOON SHOES (a spring shoe), BLAM BOMB (a black bomb\nwith a lit fuse), GOLD BALL (a gold ball with a shine). The same icons show on the players' plates with a countdown.\n\n### 10.5 The Blam Tour\n\nPROLOGUE → STOP 1 → STOP 2 → STOP 3 → THE REVEAL → THE FINAL → ENDING → CREDITS → HALL OF BLAM ENTRY.\n\n| You pick | Stop 1 | Stop 2 | Stop 3 | Final |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hightops | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Breakers | Hightops at the Skybox | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Crushers | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Magma | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n\n- CPU difficulty: the Settings value (default Pro) shifted by stop: stop 1 one step lower, stop 2 as set, stop 3 half a\n  step higher, the final one step higher (clamped to BLAM).\n- Power-ups off at stop 1, on from stop 2. Quarters 1:30. One or two players (a second human joins on the same team at\n  the Tour's team select).\n- Each stop: tour map → matchup card (codes) → pre-game talk → tip-off → the game → results → post-game beat → map\n  (autosave). A loss: results → REMATCH? 10-second countdown (Rematch, Tour Map, Quit Tour); a rematch replays the stop.\n- Tour score = the stops' style points (wins only). At the end, or on quitting after a loss, a qualifying score enters\n  the Hall of Blam (`E.Arcade` initials wheel).\n\n### 10.6 Story script (`04-data-story.js`)\n\nTone: a loud 90s sports broadcast. Announcers speak in ALL CAPS, punchy, pun-heavy; the Commissioner is smug and speaks\nin sentence case; robots speak in SPACED. CAPITAL. WORDS. `{TEAM}` is your team's name; `{CAPTAIN}` your first player.\nBeats play in engine scenes (§11.3) as `E.Dialog` lines with live portraits and voices, staged with posed rigs and camera\nmoves (`game.script`, `game.tween`). Hold confirm 1 s to skip a beat, Start to skip all of it.\n\n1. **prologue** (the Channel BLAM studio desk; the Commissioner on a monitor)\n   - VINNIE: \"GOOD EVENING, BALL FANS! LIVE FROM THE TOP OF THE WORLD, THIS IS CHANNEL BLAM!\"\n   - DEE DEE: \"AND THIS IS THE BLAM TOUR! FIVE COURTS! FOUR CREWS! ONE GOLDEN BLAMBOOZLE! ZERO FOULS!\"\n   - VINNIE: \"TONIGHT'S TOUR IS SPONSORED BY GLOBO-BLAM CORP. THEY MAKE EVERYTHING. THEY MADE THIS SENTENCE.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Greetings, little ballers. Win my Tour and the Golden Blamboozle is yours.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Lose, and your court becomes a GLOBO-BLAM parking lot. Validated parking, of course. Ha. Ha. Ha.\"\n   - DEE DEE: \"{TEAM}, THE WHOLE CITY IS WATCHING. NO PRESSURE! EXCEPT ALL OF IT!\"\n2. **camp-offer** (first Tour only) — DEE DEE: \"FIRST TIME ON THE TOUR? HIT BLAM CAMP AND I'LL SHOW YOU THE ROPES. OR\n   DON'T. LIVE DANGEROUSLY!\" Choices: BLAM CAMP / LET'S PLAY.\n3. **stop intro** (each stop, at the court) — VINNIE: \"STOP {N} OF THE BLAM TOUR: {HOME} VERSUS {AWAY} AT {COURT}!\" plus\n   DEE DEE's court line: Skybox \"THIRTY STORIES UP AND THE NETS ARE STILL SMOKING!\"; Pier \"WATCH THE WIND, FOLKS. AND THE\n   SEAGULLS. MOSTLY THE SEAGULLS.\"; Scrapyard \"OIL ON THE FLOOR AND FIRE IN THEIR EYES!\"; Caldera \"THE FLOOR IS HOT, THE\n   VOLCANO IS HOTTER, AND THE MUSIC IS HOTTEST!\"; Dome \"THE BLAM DOME! SIXTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE VERY NERVOUS\n   JUMBOTRON!\"\n4. **pre-game talk** (the rival captain, then your captain's reply by team):\n   - vs Breakers — RIPTIDE: \"Hope you packed sunscreen, {TEAM}. The tide's coming in, and it doesn't knock.\" Replies:\n     VOLT \"Cute pier. I'm about to dunk on it.\" · TORQUE \"I've crushed bigger boats than this.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Sand turns\n     to glass when I'm around.\"\n   - vs Hightops — VOLT: \"Welcome to the Skybox. Try not to look down. Actually, look down: that's where you'll be.\"\n     Replies: RIPTIDE \"Whoa, relax. We're just here to ride the wave. Over you.\" · TORQUE \"Fancy lights. They'll look\n     great on my scrap pile.\" · EMBER \"Neon's cute. Lava's hotter.\"\n   - vs Crushers — TORQUE: \"We crush cars for breakfast. You look like a light snack.\" Replies: VOLT \"Then you're about\n     to get a stomachache.\" · SHELLSHOCK \"Careful, the floor's greasier than your jokes.\" · PUMICE \"I bounce. You crush.\n     Let's see who's still standing.\"\n   - vs Magma — OBSIDIAN: \"On Kaboom Island the floor is lava. Not a game. Actual lava. Walk carefully.\" Replies:\n     BIG RUMBLE \"I don't walk carefully. I walk LOUD.\" · RIPTIDE \"Dude. Is that, like, safe?\" · SPARKPLUG \"I'm too fast\n     to get burned!\"\n5. **post-game, stop 1** — the beaten captain: RIPTIDE \"Wipeout. Totally gnarly, though. Respect.\" · VOLT \"Okay, okay.\n   You can ball. Don't let it go to your head.\" · TORQUE \"You crushed us. That's MY job.\" · OBSIDIAN \"The mountain...\n   respects you.\" Then GIGAWATT (monitor): \"Hmm. Promising. My engineers are taking notes. Lots of notes.\"\n6. **post-game, stop 2** — GIGAWATT: \"Data received. Prototype calibration at ninety-eight percent. Keep playing,\n   little ballers. Keep... teaching them.\" DEE DEE: \"TEACHING WHO? VINNIE, WHY DOES THE GLOBO-BLAM LOGO HAVE A ROBOT\n   ARM?\" VINNIE: \"THAT'S BRANDING, DEE DEE. WE DON'T ASK QUESTIONS ON LIVE TV.\"\n7. **the reveal** (after stop 3, at the Dome, the Commissioner in person)\n   - VINNIE: \"THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Congratulations. You have earned the privilege... of being replaced.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Behold the future of basketball: the BLAMBOTS! No salaries! No sweat! No mercy!\"\n   - DUNKATRON: \"BEEP. YOUR. CAREER. IS. DEPRECATED.\"\n   - SWATBOT: \"INITIATING. TRASH. TALK. PROTOCOL. ... YOU. STINK.\"\n   - {CAPTAIN} by team: VOLT \"Did the toaster just trash-talk me?\" · RIPTIDE \"Bummer. I was gonna say we could be\n     friends.\" · TORQUE \"I've got a crusher with your names on it.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Metal melts.\"\n8. **final pre-game** — VINNIE: \"THE FINAL! HUMANS VERSUS HARDWARE! THE BLAMBOOZLE IS ON THE LINE!\"\n9. **overclock** (in play, captions and the jumbotron) — GIGAWATT: \"OVERCLOCK THEM! MAXIMUM BLAM!\" DEE DEE: \"THE ROBOTS\n   ARE GLOWING! IS THAT LEGAL? THERE ARE NO RULES! I FORGOT!\"\n10. **first reboot** (in play, once) — DEE DEE: \"THEY SHORT-CIRCUIT WHEN YOU KNOCK THEM DOWN! KEEP SHOVING, {TEAM}!\"\n11. **ending** (after winning the final)\n    - DUNKATRON: \"ERROR. ERROR. HUMANS. TOO. ... BLAM.\" (sparks; both bots topple)\n    - VINNIE: \"THEY DID IT! {TEAM} WINS THE BLAM TOUR!\"\n    - DEE DEE: \"AND THE BLAMBOTS ARE BEING RECYCLED INTO VERY SAD TOASTERS!\"\n    - GIGAWATT: \"This isn't over! I'll buy another league! I'll buy the MOON! Hey! Put me down!\" (BLAMMO carries the\n      Commissioner off over a shoulder)\n    - VINNIE: \"STREETBALL IS SAVED! THE BLAMBOOZLE GOES HOME WITH {TEAM}!\"\n    - DEE DEE: \"GOODNIGHT, EVERYBODY! REMEMBER: NO FOULS! NO MERCY!\" VINNIE and DEE DEE: \"ALL BLAM!\"\n12. **credits** — scrolling credits over the trophy lift and a crowd confetti storm, the `credits` song; then unlock\n    cards: \"UNLOCKED: THE BLAMBOTS\", \"UNLOCKED: CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS\", \"UNLOCKED: BIG HEADS (OPTIONS)\", \"SECRETS ON\n    THE ABOUT SCREEN\".\n13. **losses** — stops 1–3: GIGAWATT \"Tsk. Another court for my parking empire.\" The final: GIGAWATT \"Resistance is...\n    adorable.\" DUNKATRON \"GAME. OVER. INSERT. COIN.\"\n14. **halftime gags** (one per halftime, no repeats within a Tour): \"THIS HALFTIME IS BROUGHT TO YOU BY GLOBO-BLAM\n    SNEAKER GLUE. STICK THE LANDING. FOREVER.\" · \"OUR STATS DEPARTMENT IS ONE GUY WITH A CALCULATOR, AND HE IS\n    SWEATING.\" · \"REMEMBER, KIDS: STAY IN SCHOOL. AND IN THE PAINT.\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM COLA: NOW WITH 30% MORE FIZZ AND 0%\n    EXPLANATION.\" · \"IF YOU'RE JUST JOINING US: YES, THAT WAS A REAL DUNK. NO, WE DON'T KNOW HOW EITHER.\" · \"WE ASKED THE\n    ROBOTS FOR A HALFTIME COMMENT. THEY SENT US A RECEIPT.\"\n15. **sponsor breaks** (one per shatter) — \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK AFTER THIS MESSAGE FROM GLOBO-BLAM GLASS: NOW 40% LESS\n    SHATTERY!\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM INSURANCE: BECAUSE SOMEBODY HAS TO PAY FOR THAT.\" · \"THIS REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD IS BROUGHT\n    TO YOU BY... THE LAST REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD.\"\n\n### 10.7 Announcer lines (`05-data-lines.js`)\n\nBanks by event, at least 10 lines each (write them in the voice of the samples), ALL CAPS, at most 60 characters a\nline, with `{NAME}`, `{VICTIM}`, `{TEAM}` slots. Rules: big plays interrupt small ones; at most two captions per\npossession; no line repeats within the last 8; per-bank cooldowns; Settings → Commentary (Full, Big plays, Off). VINNIE\ncalls the play, DEE DEE adds the color; alternate them. Samples:\n\n| Bank | Samples |\n|---|---|\n| tipoff | \"WELCOME TO CHANNEL BLAM! LET'S GET LOUD!\" · \"THE BALL IS UP! THE CROWD IS UP! I AM UP!\" |\n| dunk (power) | \"BLAMMO! {NAME} JUST MAILED IT FIRST CLASS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL A CARPENTER, THAT RIM IS FINISHED!\" · \"KA-BLAM! THE CROWD LEFT THEIR SEATS. AND THEIR SHOES!\" |\n| dunk (spin, flip, hang, long) | \"{NAME} SPUN SO FAST THE SCOREBOARD GOT DIZZY!\" · \"A FRONT FLIP?! THAT'S NOT BASKETBALL, THAT'S THE CIRCUS!\" · \"{NAME} IS HANGING ON THAT RIM LIKE IT OWES MONEY!\" · \"AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL HAS QUESTIONS FOR {NAME}!\" |\n| alley-oop | \"SPECIAL DELIVERY! SIGNED, SEALED, SLAMMED!\" |\n| three / deep three | \"SPLASH! BRING A TOWEL!\" · \"THAT WAS FROM A DIFFERENT ZIP CODE!\" · \"{NAME} SHOT THAT FROM THE PARKING LOT! VALIDATED!\" |\n| airball | \"AIRBALL! THE SEAGULLS SAY THANK YOU!\" · \"THAT ONE IS STILL GOING. IT'S IN ORBIT.\" |\n| block | \"REJECTED! RETURN TO SENDER!\" · \"{NAME} SAYS NOT IN MY HOUSE, NOT IN MY YARD, NOT IN MY ZIP CODE!\" |\n| steal | \"PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!\" · \"{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!\" |\n| shove | \"NO FOULS IN BASKETBLAM, BABY!\" · \"THAT'S NOT A FOUL. THAT'S A LIFESTYLE.\" · \"{VICTIM} JUST GOT SENT TO THE SHADOW REALM!\" |\n| ankles | \"ANKLES! {VICTIM} NEEDS A NEW PAIR!\" |\n| posterized | \"FRAME IT! HANG IT! {VICTIM} IS ON {NAME}'S WALL NOW!\" |\n| Supernova on / off | \"{NAME} HAS GONE SUPERNOVA! DIM THE LIGHTS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL NASA, {NAME} IS A STAR!\" · \"AND THE STAR COLLAPSES! BACK TO EARTH, {NAME}!\" |\n| shatter | \"THE GLASS! THE GLASS IS GONE!\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A BROOM. A BIGGER BROOM!\" |\n| goaltend | \"GOALTENDING! THE BUCKET COUNTS, AND SO DOES THE SHAME!\" |\n| jackpot | \"JACKPOT! {NAME} HIT THE SPOT AND THE SPOT PAID OUT!\" |\n| power-ups | \"ROCKET KICKS! {NAME} IS LEGALLY A VEHICLE NOW!\" · \"GLUE GLOVES! THAT BALL ISN'T GOING ANYWHERE!\" · \"LASER SIGHT! {NAME} CAN SEE THE FUTURE, AND IT'S A BUCKET!\" · \"MOON SHOES! GRAVITY HAS LEFT THE BUILDING!\" · \"BLAM BOMB! EVERYBODY DUCK!\" · \"GOLD BALL! NEXT BUCKET'S WORTH DOUBLE!\" |\n| clutch / buzzer | \"TEN SECONDS! HEARTS POUNDING! SNEAKERS SQUEAKING!\" · \"AT THE BUZZER! I BROKE MY CHAIR! I NEED A NEW CHAIR!\" |\n| comeback / blowout | \"{TEAM} IS CLAWING BACK! DON'T TOUCH THAT DIAL!\" · \"THIS ONE'S GETTING UGLY. I'M COVERING MY EYES. I'M PEEKING.\" |\n| twists | \"BIG GUST OFF THE OCEAN! HOLD ONTO YOUR HATS AND YOUR JUMPERS!\" · \"{NAME} HIT THE OIL! THAT'S A SLIP 'N SLAM!\" · \"THE VOLCANO WANTS IN ON THE ACTION!\" · \"{NAME} RODE THE STEAM VENT TO THE MOON!\" |\n| boss | \"THE ROBOTS ARE OVERCLOCKING! SMELLS LIKE BURNT TOAST IN HERE!\" · \"SYSTEM REBOOT! TURN IT OFF AND ON AGAIN, BABY!\" · \"THOSE ROBOTS RUN ON BATTERIES AND BAD MANNERS!\" |\n| shot clock | \"SHOT CLOCK! YOU HAVE TO SHOOT IT EVENTUALLY, FOLKS!\" |\n| quarter end / halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE QUARTER! CATCH YOUR BREATH, I CAN'T!\" · \"HALFTIME! STRETCH YOUR LEGS AND YOUR VOCABULARY!\" · \"FINAL! {TEAM} TAKES IT!\" |\n\nPlayers also bark short trash talk when they taunt, dunk on someone or get a steal (3–5 lines each in their own voice,\ne.g. VOLT \"Too slow!\", BIG RUMBLE \"Move.\", SPARKPLUG \"Mine now!\", DUNKATRON \"BALL. ACQUIRED.\").\n\n### 10.8 Cheat codes and unlocks","numLines":420,"startLine":578,"totalLines":1605}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QQikXYb83inveSYhsZPfcr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
