{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2sDvtAV6vgUtWmzgkv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FCRJcvWU62SkFVdrSSaacv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-061830__x5a4f79/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nei = {\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 06:18:30\",\n    \"source\": \"Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports: 2-on-2 basketball in the over-the-top arcade style, with a four-stop story tour\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Side-on broadcast camera (custom orthographic view, pitch 30 degrees, panning with the ball), with an optional High (three-quarter) camera\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified copy, changes marked in the engine); AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified); plain JavaScript; Canvas 2D; Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast: five courts (neon Skybox, sunset Pier, dusk Scrapyard, night Caldera, arena Blam Dome), new courts, props, crowds and lighting\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs posed by math; a hand layer (inverse kinematics) for the ball; a procedural dribble synced to the ball; the engine's moves; a dunk path with per-dunk banners\",\n    \"audio\": \"All music, sound effects and voices written in code: 12 songs, 8 stings, about 90 sound effects, a crowd ambience, and gibberish formant voices with captions\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN): host-authoritative snapshots, input messages, the hub's card, leave, time-up and end handling, a server copy\",\n    \"testing\": \"76 headless tests (content, physics, rules, mechanics, ai, determinism, flow, ui, audio, net, camp, tour, attract, dev, bundle) via node:vm; 3 browser tests (Playwright); the AI Hub harness: 2 of its 4 scenarios pass, 2 do not complete (see testingFeedback)\",\n    \"research\": \"none\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for the tests: Chromium; the player's browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"About 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour of session time\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 15 issues, found by the tests, the browser run and the hub harness; four were game-breaking: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start without a body for the canvas\",\n    \"Four game-breaking issues (above), the rest minor: a long announcer line, a menu draw outside its overlay, a voice that read gap syllables, and the card answering 'more time' to Enter\",\n    \"The full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with the event counts: they exposed most of the bugs that unit checks missed\",\n    \"The hub harness as a black box: when two of its scenarios stalled it gave no cause, so we ran instrumented copies, and we did not find the cause of the two stalls\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The HD rigs and the look out of the box; E.TileMap with floorTex; game.advance for fixed steps in tests; E.Dialog; the input labels and glyph names\",\n    \"Yes: E.arc's apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height (first guessed wrong); the canvas needs document.body, so the scripts must sit at the end of body (a crash until fixed); we guessed the rig's hand joints from solvePose\",\n    \"The shot model and its decided outcomes, the ball physics against the arena, rims and glass, the CPU brains, the match flow and the netcode, the voices and the songs\",\n    \"The ball against the rims and the arena walls, and posing a rig's hand from a target (the pose internals were not documented)\",\n    \"Four changes, each marked /* BASKETBLAM: ... */: public audio buses (sfxBus, musicBus); basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function. Each was needed for the game's look or its voices\",\n    \"A public hook for a rig's hand targets (so a pose layer needs no solvePose wrapping), and a canvas that is created on demand instead of needing document.body at script time\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The milestones, the tables of numbers and the list of tests: a clear target to build and check against\",\n    \"The goal and STAGE.md name the folder and the file differently, and the title came from the plan's pick rather than a pick of this run\",\n    \"The scope in one session: eleven milestones, about 230 tests and a hub check\",\n    \"Split it into a playable core first and the polish after, and give the hub check its own budget\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"BASKETBLAM\",\n    \"tagline\": \"No fouls. No mercy. All BLAM.\",\n    \"description\": \"Over-the-top 2-on-2 arcade basketball on five courts with dunks, shoves, Supernova and a story tour against the robot Blambots. Up to four players, on one screen or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Basketball (over-the-top arcade style)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD moves · Square or Space shoots · Cross or E passes · R2 or Shift turbo · Circle or Q shoves · Triangle or F lobs\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]\n  }\n}\nwith open('exit-interview.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(ei, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    f.write('\\n')\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('valid JSON; testing feedback items', len(ei['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(ei['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(ei['promptFeedback']))\nEOF\nnode -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('node parse ok')\"","description":"Write and validate the exit interview JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4601,"cache_read_input_tokens":689672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4601},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"dcc13f26-94fc-473d-a7a2-2cf93f207c62","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:53.729Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2sDbo1ZERPCnfmHeTz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FCRJcvWU62SkFVdrSSaacv":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-061830__x5a4f79/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nei = {\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 06:18:30\",\n    \"source\": \"Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports: 2-on-2 basketball in the over-the-top arcade style, with a four-stop story tour\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Side-on broadcast camera (custom orthographic view, pitch 30 degrees, panning with the ball), with an optional High (three-quarter) camera\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified copy, changes marked in the engine); AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified); plain JavaScript; Canvas 2D; Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast: five courts (neon Skybox, sunset Pier, dusk Scrapyard, night Caldera, arena Blam Dome), new courts, props, crowds and lighting\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs posed by math; a hand layer (inverse kinematics) for the ball; a procedural dribble synced to the ball; the engine's moves; a dunk path with per-dunk banners\",\n    \"audio\": \"All music, sound effects and voices written in code: 12 songs, 8 stings, about 90 sound effects, a crowd ambience, and gibberish formant voices with captions\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN): host-authoritative snapshots, input messages, the hub's card, leave, time-up and end handling, a server copy\",\n    \"testing\": \"76 headless tests (content, physics, rules, mechanics, ai, determinism, flow, ui, audio, net, camp, tour, attract, dev, bundle) via node:vm; 3 browser tests (Playwright); the AI Hub harness: 2 of its 4 scenarios pass, 2 do not complete (see testingFeedback)\",\n    \"research\": \"none\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for the tests: Chromium; the player's browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"About 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour of session time\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 15 issues, found by the tests, the browser run and the hub harness; four were game-breaking: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start without a body for the canvas\",\n    \"Four game-breaking issues (above), the rest minor: a long announcer line, a menu draw outside its overlay, a voice that read gap syllables, and the card answering 'more time' to Enter\",\n    \"The full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with the event counts: they exposed most of the bugs that unit checks missed\",\n    \"The hub harness as a black box: when two of its scenarios stalled it gave no cause, so we ran instrumented copies, and we did not find the cause of the two stalls\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The HD rigs and the look out of the box; E.TileMap with floorTex; game.advance for fixed steps in tests; E.Dialog; the input labels and glyph names\",\n    \"Yes: E.arc's apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height (first guessed wrong); the canvas needs document.body, so the scripts must sit at the end of body (a crash until fixed); we guessed the rig's hand joints from solvePose\",\n    \"The shot model and its decided outcomes, the ball physics against the arena, rims and glass, the CPU brains, the match flow and the netcode, the voices and the songs\",\n    \"The ball against the rims and the arena walls, and posing a rig's hand from a target (the pose internals were not documented)\",\n    \"Four changes, each marked /* BASKETBLAM: ... */: public audio buses (sfxBus, musicBus); basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function. Each was needed for the game's look or its voices\",\n    \"A public hook for a rig's hand targets (so a pose layer needs no solvePose wrapping), and a canvas that is created on demand instead of needing document.body at script time\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The milestones, the tables of numbers and the list of tests: a clear target to build and check against\",\n    \"The goal and STAGE.md name the folder and the file differently, and the title came from the plan's pick rather than a pick of this run\",\n    \"The scope in one session: eleven milestones, about 230 tests and a hub check\",\n    \"Split it into a playable core first and the polish after, and give the hub check its own budget\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"BASKETBLAM\",\n    \"tagline\": \"No fouls. No mercy. All BLAM.\",\n    \"description\": \"Over-the-top 2-on-2 arcade basketball on five courts with dunks, shoves, Supernova and a story tour against the robot Blambots. Up to four players, on one screen or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Basketball (over-the-top arcade style)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD moves · Square or Space shoots · Cross or E passes · R2 or Shift turbo · Circle or Q shoves · Triangle or F lobs\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]\n  }\n}\nwith open('exit-interview.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(ei, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    f.write('\\n')\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('valid JSON; testing feedback items', len(ei['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(ei['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(ei['promptFeedback']))\nEOF\nnode -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('node parse ok')\"","description":"Write and validate the exit interview JSON"}}}
