{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi45sxpcqBichNwwzrJh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The title is now the drawn one, ZONEFIRE, and the gaps from the last round are closed. The stop condition still isn't fully met, and the animation gap at the end says so.\n\n**Closed this round**\n- **Title:** drawn with a real RNG (`secrets.randbelow`) from a list of exactly 50 candidates. The draw was ZONEFIRE. The game, its file names, the dev folder and the exit interview are renamed to match.\n- **Per-player SUB screen:** at each break, a human side gets a picker. Up and down choose who comes off, left and right choose who comes on, confirm makes the change, and cancel keeps the team as it is. CPU sides still sub automatically.\n- **Blam Camp rules card:** lesson 10 ends on a six-line rules card that the player confirms.\n- **Voice volume:** now a real slider (0 to 1, step 0.1) using the engine's slider type.\n- **Session overlay:** tested in a hub-flagged match. It opens and closes on cancel, and the simulation keeps advancing while it is open.\n- **Full Blam Tour:** a test plays all four stops through the scenes, with the matchup, the match, the results and the beats, and ends with the BLAMBOTS and ALL-STARS unlocked.\n\n**Verification:** 79 headless tests, 3 browser tests and 4 hub harness scenarios all pass on the final build. The hub's two earlier stalls were a mistake in my test, which omitted `auto=1`; the game was not at fault.\n\n**Still not met**\n- **Dunk and body animation:** the hand keyframes, spins and flip are a simplified version of the plan's per-dunk clips. Celebrations and taunts all use the engine's single cheer pose.\n- **Pass, steal and shove:** these have no separate wind-up clips.\n- **Presentation extras:** the pause menu is not themed, and the tour map is a simple painted map.\n\nThese are animation-fidelity gaps against the plan, not missing systems. The stop condition needs them closed before it can be met.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE); the plan's own title was BASKETBLAM and was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math; a hand layer for the ball; a procedural dribble; per-dunk hand keys, spins and a flip\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 79 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hand from a target.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a public hook for a rig's hand targets, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount when listing candidates.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1510,"cache_read_input_tokens":768291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1510},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"50d4a1d6-ba79-414d-bb24-bf9d26474c06","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:34:51.249Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi45sbVL6FPmjMBCzou2"}
