{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4Eke3KNzeq8sueFtZj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop condition is not met. The bundled HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in place and the JSON parses. The required sections are in this reply. Several PLAN.md features are still unbuilt or simplified, and I've listed them below rather than claim them done.\n\n**Done this round**\n- Pass, steal and shove now have short wind-up and strike poses, so they no longer share one stance.\n- The tour map has a skyline, a sea, and labels.\n- The Blam Camp rules card, the voice volume slider and the per-player SUB screen were completed in the previous round.\n\n**Still open against PLAN.md**\n- **Dunk body animation:** each dunk has hand keyframes, and the 360 and 720 dunks spin. The plan's per-dunk body clips are not built.\n- **Celebrations and taunts:** these all use the engine's single cheer pose.\n- **Pause menu:** it is the engine's default, not the themed Shell the plan specifies.\n- **Tour map:** it is a simple painted map, not the plan's full map.\n\n**Verification on this build:** 79 headless tests pass, 3 browser tests pass, and the four AI Hub harness scenarios passed on the previous build.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE). The plan's own title (BASKETBLAM) was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math; a hand layer for the ball; a procedural dribble; wind-up and strike poses for pass, steal and shove; per-dunk hand keys, spins and a flip. Not built: per-dunk body clips, separate celebration and taunt clips.\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 79 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hand from a target.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a public hook for a rig's hand targets, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount when listing candidates.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":775341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":938},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"fb9b34a4-205b-4d4b-94dc-a61c244fd1d1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:36:47.486Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4EkEyxnmPNkWpUJGaP"}
