{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi54TbT4i2hV1edx5Nhv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop condition is still not met, and I can't honestly claim it is.\n\n**Closed this round**\n- **Pause menu:** replaced the engine's pause screen with our own, drawn in the game's UI kit. It offers Resume, Settings, Controls, How to Play, Restart, Dev Mode (not in hub rounds) and Quit to title. It freezes the match while open, and a test covers opening, freezing and resuming. The earlier bug was the opening press also closing the menu in the same frame.\n\n**Still open against PLAN.md**\n- **Full-body per-dunk clips.** Each dunk has hand keyframes, a crouch before takeoff, a slam kick, a cheer, a landing, spins and a flip. A full-body clip per dunk is not built.\n- **Full-body celebration and taunt clips.** These are named hand poses, not full-body moves.\n\nBoth need a decision on scope. Building them would mean inventing the animation design rather than following the plan closely. Tell me whether to build them, or to accept them as the known gap.\n\n**Verification on the final bundle:** 80 headless tests, 3 browser tests and 4 hub scenarios pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE). The plan's own title (BASKETBLAM) was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; the pause menu is drawn in our own UI kit\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math; a hand layer for the ball; a procedural dribble; wind-ups for pass, steal and shove; named celebrations and taunts; per-dunk hand keys, body crouch, slam kick and landing, spins and a flip\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 80 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios, all passing on the final build\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hand from a target.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a public hook for a rig's hand targets, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount when listing candidates.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":812576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"31d715fc-bbd5-4935-9dfe-8aaae0fa73a7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:47:35.054Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi54T9fV2FrKXSBgyfza"}
