{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5PguRaBk2dbRM2URan","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built the remaining items. The plan's body clips are now keyframed, but the engine's rig has no free lean control, so lean is not animated, and that is the one limitation I'll flag.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Full-body clips:** every celebration, taunt and dunk is a keyframed clip over both hands, the body's height, the rig's pose and a squash. The left hand now has its own pose layer.\n- **Dunks:** each dunk has its own clip, so the crouch, slam kick, cheer and landing come from the clip.\n\n**Verification on the final bundle:** 81 headless tests, 3 browser tests and 4 hub harness scenarios pass.\n\n**Known limitation:** the rig exposes no free lean control, so lean is not animated.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE). The plan's own title (BASKETBLAM) was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; the pause menu is drawn in our own UI kit\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math. Each celebration, taunt and dunk is a keyframed body clip over both hands, the body's height, pose and squash. Also a hand layer for the ball, a procedural dribble, and wind-ups for pass, steal and shove. The rig exposes no free lean, so lean is not animated.\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 81 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios; all passing on the final build\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`, and the rig exposes no free lean control.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hands from targets.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a public hook for a rig's hand targets and body lean, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount when listing candidates.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":828975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":984},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"023d0504-cd24-49a3-b933-ec7af1766fa8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:51:56.523Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5PgXbs2YbQH2p7YcQy"}
