{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5a33faVncmpXn6kxm4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've closed the lean gap. The rig now reads the lean value each frame, so the dunk and celebration clips lean the body. Every suite passes on the final bundle: 81 headless, 3 browser and 4 hub scenarios.\n\nI still can't certify that every PLAN.md line is built. The plan is about 1,600 lines, and I have not checked each line against the build. Below is the TASK.md checklist with the evidence for each item, and the points where I implemented something smaller than the plan.\n\n**TASK.md checklist**\n- **Single HTML file in root:** done; `Zonefire-Basketball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-061830.html`.\n- **Source, genre, perspective:** done; broadcast camera with optional High view.\n- **Title by RNG from 50:** done; ZONEFIRE, drawn with `secrets.randbelow` from a 50-item list. (My first two drawn lists had the wrong count, so the draw used a corrected list.)\n- **Built on the engine handoff:** done; engine copy with marked edits.\n- **Art, animation, audio, voices:** done; all audio is generated in code, and voices are gibberish with captions. Animation is keyed clips for celebrations, taunts and dunks, plus pass, steal and shove wind-ups.\n- **AI Hub multiplayer:** done; all four harness scenarios pass.\n- **Dev mode with sliders and reset:** done; every tuning value is a slider, with reset.\n- **Attract mode:** done; five segments, any input exits.\n- **10-foot UI, glyphs, touch-only notice:** done; PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, keyboard and mouse, touch-only notice.\n- **Source info and feedback in About and reply:** done.\n- **No TODOs, placeholders or stubs:** a grep of the source finds none.\n\n**Where I built something smaller than the plan**\n- **Pause menu:** our own, drawn in the game's UI kit, with the engine's settings and controls screens behind it. It does not use the plan's custom Shell design.\n- **Tour map:** landmarks, medallions with W stamps, hover and click, and a side panel with score, record and next opponent. It is simpler than the plan's map.\n- **Pass, steal and shove:** short hand-based wind-ups, not full-body clips.\n- **Lean:** driven by the clips through the rig's lean option. This is a small engine read, marked as ours.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE). The plan's own title (BASKETBLAM) was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; the pause menu is drawn in our own UI kit\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math. Each celebration, taunt and dunk is a keyframed body clip over both hands, the body's height, pose, lean and squash. Also a hand layer for the ball, a procedural dribble, and wind-ups for pass, steal and shove.\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 81 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios; all run on the final build\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`. The lean option is read each frame, but only through an undocumented path.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hands from targets.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a documented hook for a rig's hand targets and lean, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount when listing candidates.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":886,"cache_read_input_tokens":837531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":886},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"a0e8a414-5c6d-4336-a641-3155956716e6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:54:18.683Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5a2aszBeDd86CGVmgb"}
