{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5ayC2PZYWQDRvA5j5A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't meet this condition as written, and I'm not going to keep re-declaring it done.\n\n**What is actually verified:** the bundled HTML exists in the work folder root, `exit-interview.json` parses, and the four sections are below. On the final bundle, 81 headless tests, 3 browser tests and 4 hub harness scenarios pass.\n\n**What is not verified:** I have not checked every PLAN.md line against the build. Known simplifications against the plan are:\n- The pause menu is our own UI-kit menu, not the plan's custom Shell design.\n- The tour map is simpler than the plan's map.\n- Pass, steal and shove use hand-only wind-ups, not full-body clips.\n\n**What I need from you:** the stop condition asks for a full line-by-line check of PLAN.md. That would be a multi-hour audit plus rebuilding the three items above. Either you tell me to do that, or you accept this build with those three named gaps as the finished state. Until you choose, I can't truthfully report the full-implementation requirement as met.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md. The title was drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates (ZONEFIRE), after an earlier draw used the wrong candidate count. The plan's own title (BASKETBLAM) was replaced.\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera (orthographic pitch 30), with an optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art direction:** the engine's HD style pushed to 90s arcade broadcast, with five courts\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs posed by math; keyed body clips for celebrations, taunts and dunks; a hand layer for the ball; a procedural dribble; hand-only wind-ups for pass, steal and shove\n- **Audio:** music, effects and voices made in code; gibberish voices with captions\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world session (HUB SHOWDOWN), with a session overlay that does not pause\n- **Testing:** 81 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub harness scenarios; all pass on the final build\n- **Research:** none\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser for tests: Chromium\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.7M tokens by the session's budget counter; API cost in USD unknown; about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four: a ball trapped on the rim's centre, a quarter that never ended, players stuck in their jump, and the page failing to start.\n- **Most helpful test:** full CPU-vs-CPU matches to the final whistle, with event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** the hub harness as a black box. Its two stalls named no cause, and the fault was in my own test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the HD rigs out of the box, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests, and `E.Dialog`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `E.arc`'s apex is the rise over the higher end, not an absolute height. The canvas needs `document.body`, so the scripts must sit at the end of the body. The hand joints had to be read from `solvePose`, and lean is read each frame through an undocumented option.\n- **Built ourselves:** the shot model, ball physics, CPU brains, match flow, netcode, voices and songs.\n- **Hardest:** the ball against the rims and arena walls, and posing a rig's hands from targets.\n- **Engine changes** (each marked `/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): audio buses `sfxBus` and `musicBus`; basketball shorts on the HD legs; hair styles afro, flattop and mohawk; a Dialog voice that may be a function.\n- **One change to make:** a documented hook for a rig's hand targets and lean, so a pose layer needs no reading of `solvePose`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the milestones, the number tables and the test list.\n- **Confusing:** the goal and STAGE.md name the folder and file differently, and the brainstorm rule (\"fifty titles\") is easy to miscount.\n- **Hardest:** the scope in one session: eleven milestones and about 230 tests in the plan.\n- **Would change:** build a playable core first and polish after, and give the hub check its own budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2689,"cache_read_input_tokens":838417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2689},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0432b045-5008-4207-9914-efcb595d2dad","uuid":"f40ddd89-78f3-469d-8876-7b597d6402a9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:54:29.999Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5axiVwxf9kA1EkrbFS"}
