d | Pass | My hub servers were stopped by PID; other agents' servers were left alone. |\n\nThe stop condition still isn't fully met: the line-by-line audit of PLAN.md's prose and the rendered tour-map comparison are not done. Those are the two items I said were open, and the table shows which parts are fully and partly checked.\n\nThe bundled HTML is in the work folder root, and `exit-interview.json` parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:18:30\n- **Source:** Basketball, over-the-top arcade style (genre inspiration; an original game)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md; title ZONEFIRE drawn this run with a real RNG from 50 candidates\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball; side-on broadcast camera, optional High camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified), AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio\n- **Testing:** 80 headless, 3 browser, 4 hub scenarios; all pass on the final build\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- About 15 issues caught, four game-breaking. Most helpful: full CPU-vs-CPU matches. Least helpful: the hub harness as a black box; its stalls came from my test's missing `auto=1`.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- Liked most: the HD rigs, `E.TileMap` with `floorTex`, `game.advance` for headless tests. Stuck on `E.arc`'s apex being a rise, and on the canvas needing `document.body`. One change: a documented hook for hand targets and lean.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- Liked most: the milestones and test list. Confusing: the folder and file naming differs between the goal and STAGE.md. Would change: build a playable core first, then polish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1205,"cache_read_input_tokens":879273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1205},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":